{"jobs":[{"id":"efe55756-f28b-4030-b9a0-539f6c8ed8ff","title":"Engineering Manager, Platform","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-10-12T20:53:19.718+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/airbyte/efe55756-f28b-4030-b9a0-539f6c8ed8ff","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/airbyte/efe55756-f28b-4030-b9a0-539f6c8ed8ff/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Airbyte is the data and action layer for AI agents. We give agents fast, accurate, authenticated access to business data across hundreds of sources, so they can discover the entities that matter, reason over real-time context, and take action in the systems they read from, not just observe them.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We started as the open-source standard for data movement and proved the economics of data integration at scale: hundreds of connectors, thousands of companies, and, since 2020, have raised $181M from leading investors including Benchmark, Accel, Altimeter, Coatue, and Y Combinator. As our CEO Michel Tricot puts it, \"the last ten years were all about structured data. The future is all about context.\" We're now building that context infrastructure for production-grade agents on the same open foundation, as agents become the primary consumers of enterprise data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our mission is unchanged: make data available and actionable to everyone, everywhere. That everyone now includes AI agents.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>The Role:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Airbyte is looking for an Engineering Manager, Platform to lead the team responsible for the infrastructure, tooling, and engineering systems that power Airbyte Cloud, Airbyte Flex, and Airbyte Agents.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As an Engineering Manager on the Platform team, you'll lead the engineers responsible for cloud infrastructure, deployment systems, CI/CD, observability, reliability, and the internal tooling that powers engineering velocity across the company. Your work directly shapes both how fast engineers ship and how customers experience Airbyte. This isn't a keep-the-lights-on role. You'll make real tradeoffs between engineering velocity, customer-facing reliability, and long-term architecture every week, and you'll help define how AI transforms the way we build and operate software.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role combines people leadership, technical strategy, operational excellence, and platform thinking. You'll help define how engineering works at Airbyte - not just what we build.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h2><strong>What You’ll Do:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead, mentor, and grow a team of Platform Engineers, Fullstack Engineers, and SREs. Recruit engineers who understand that infrastructure decisions are product decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the reliability and operational health of Airbyte's production systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define the roadmap for Airbyte's platform: infrastructure, CI/CD, deployment automation, observability, internal tooling, and the product surfaces built on top of them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Invest in and drive adoption of AI-powered workflows for debugging, release validation, infrastructure management, and developer productivity, moving past experimentation into real operational leverage.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead incident response, run blameless postmortems, and ensure systemic fixes follow every outage. Continuously reduce operational toil through automation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build leverage: a week-long task this year should take ten minutes next year.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h2><strong>Success Metrics:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Engineers deploy with confidence and ship faster quarter over quarter.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Platform reliability improves as measured by customer-facing SLAs, not just internal dashboards.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Operational toil decreases through automation, not heroics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Incidents are detected faster, resolved faster, and the same failure doesn't happen twice.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Your team is engaged, growing, and building careers they're proud of.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h2><strong>What You’ll Need:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of software engineering experience, 2+ years managing engineering teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience leading Platform Engineering, Infrastructure, SRE, or Developer Productivity organizations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of cloud infrastructure, CI/CD, observability, and distributed systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience operating production systems at scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You think about platform work in terms of customer impact, not just engineering elegance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You've navigated the tension between paying down tech debt and shipping product, and you can articulate how you made those calls.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication skills. You can translate platform strategy into language that product, design, and business leaders understand.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have an insatiable desire to ship.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Nice To Have:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with AI-assisted engineering workflows or agentic software development.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building internal developer platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with Terraform, Helm, Kubernetes, GitHub Actions, and cloud-native infrastructure.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with data infrastructure, ETL/ELT, or large-scale distributed systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience contributing to open-source engineering organizations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with Airbyte, connector ecosystems, or developer tooling platforms.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h2><strong>Why This Role Matters:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Platform Engineering is the force multiplier for every engineering team at Airbyte.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Your mission is to build the systems, tooling, and infrastructure that enable engineers to move faster while making our platform more reliable, secure, and scalable. Success means every deployment becomes safer, every incident becomes easier to resolve, every engineer becomes more productive, and AI becomes a natural part of how software is built.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The best platform teams are invisible—they make everyone else dramatically more effective. That's the team you'll build.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Location:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Onsite 4 days/week in San Francisco, CA</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Why You'll Love Working at Airbyte:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Airbyte, we believe great work happens when people feel supported, trusted, and empowered to grow. Our market-leading Total Rewards package is designed to help you thrive professionally and personally. Our benefits and perks include:</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Flexible PTO with a culture that encourages at least 25 days off annually<br /> • 16 weeks fully paid parental leave for all parents<br /> • Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and dependents<br /> • 401(k) retirement plan<br /> • Professional development budget, conference sponsorship, and book reimbursement<br /> • Commuter benefits and monthly internet reimbursement</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> •  Breakfast and lunch in our San Francisco office<br /> • A collaborative, in-person culture focused on learning, growth, and impact</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you find this role exciting, we encourage you to apply even if you think you don’t meet all of the requirements!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are not accepting agency submissions or recruiting firm support for this role. Unsolicited resumes will not be considered.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Airbyte is an equal opportunity employer that does not discriminate on the basis of actual or perceived race, creed, color, religion, national origin, ancestry, age, physical or mental disability, pregnancy, genetic information, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, marital status, familial status, domestic violence victim status, veteran or military status, or any other legally recognized protected basis under federal, state or local laws. Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Airbyte is committed to providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities in our job application procedures. Please let us know if you need assistance or accommodations due to a disability.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Airbyte is the data and action layer for AI agents. We give agents fast, accurate, authenticated access to business data across hundreds of sources, so they can discover the entities that matter, reason over real-time context, and take action in the systems they read from, not just observe them.\n\n\n\nWe started as the open-source standard for data movement and proved the economics of data integration at scale: hundreds of connectors, thousands of companies, and, since 2020, have raised $181M from leading investors including Benchmark, Accel, Altimeter, Coatue, and Y Combinator. As our CEO Michel Tricot puts it, \"the last ten years were all about structured data. The future is all about context.\" We're now building that context infrastructure for production-grade agents on the same open foundation, as agents become the primary consumers of enterprise data.\n\n\n\nOur mission is unchanged: make data available and actionable to everyone, everywhere. That everyone now includes AI agents.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE:\n\nAirbyte is looking for an Engineering Manager, Platform to lead the team responsible for the infrastructure, tooling, and engineering systems that power Airbyte Cloud, Airbyte Flex, and Airbyte Agents.\n\n\n\nAs an Engineering Manager on the Platform team, you'll lead the engineers responsible for cloud infrastructure, deployment systems, CI/CD, observability, reliability, and the internal tooling that powers engineering velocity across the company. Your work directly shapes both how fast engineers ship and how customers experience Airbyte. This isn't a keep-the-lights-on role. You'll make real tradeoffs between engineering velocity, customer-facing reliability, and long-term architecture every week, and you'll help define how AI transforms the way we build and operate software.\n\n\n\nThis role combines people leadership, technical strategy, operational excellence, and platform thinking. You'll help define how engineering works at Airbyte - not just what we build.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO:\n\n - Lead, mentor, and grow a team of Platform Engineers, Fullstack Engineers, and SREs. Recruit engineers who understand that infrastructure decisions are product decisions.\n\n - Own the reliability and operational health of Airbyte's production systems.\n\n - Define the roadmap for Airbyte's platform: infrastructure, CI/CD, deployment automation, observability, internal tooling, and the product surfaces built on top of them.\n\n - Invest in and drive adoption of AI-powered workflows for debugging, release validation, infrastructure management, and developer productivity, moving past experimentation into real operational leverage.\n\n - Lead incident response, run blameless postmortems, and ensure systemic fixes follow every outage. Continuously reduce operational toil through automation.\n\n - Build leverage: a week-long task this year should take ten minutes next year.\n\n \n\n\nSUCCESS METRICS:\n\n - Engineers deploy with confidence and ship faster quarter over quarter.\n\n - Platform reliability improves as measured by customer-facing SLAs, not just internal dashboards.\n\n - Operational toil decreases through automation, not heroics.\n\n - Incidents are detected faster, resolved faster, and the same failure doesn't happen twice.\n\n - Your team is engaged, growing, and building careers they're proud of.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL NEED:\n\n - 5+ years of software engineering experience, 2+ years managing engineering teams.\n\n - Experience leading Platform Engineering, Infrastructure, SRE, or Developer Productivity organizations.\n\n - Strong understanding of cloud infrastructure, CI/CD, observability, and distributed systems.\n\n - Experience operating production systems at scale.\n\n - You think about platform work in terms of customer impact, not just engineering elegance.\n\n - You've navigated the tension between paying down tech debt and shipping product, and you can articulate how you made those calls.\n\n - Excellent communication skills. You can translate platform strategy into language that product, design, and business leaders understand.\n\n - You have an insatiable desire to ship.\n\n\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE:\n\n - Experience with AI-assisted engineering workflows or agentic software development.\n\n - Experience building internal developer platforms.\n\n - Familiarity with Terraform, Helm, Kubernetes, GitHub Actions, and cloud-native infrastructure.\n\n - Experience with data infrastructure, ETL/ELT, or large-scale distributed systems.\n\n - Experience contributing to open-source engineering organizations.\n\n - Familiarity with Airbyte, connector ecosystems, or developer tooling platforms.\n\n \n\n\nWHY THIS ROLE MATTERS:\n\nPlatform Engineering is the force multiplier for every engineering team at Airbyte.\n\n\n\nYour mission is to build the systems, tooling, and infrastructure that enable engineers to move faster while making our platform more reliable, secure, and scalable. Success means every deployment becomes safer, every incident becomes easier to resolve, every engineer becomes more productive, and AI becomes a natural part of how software is built.\n\n\n\nThe best platform teams are invisible—they make everyone else dramatically more effective. That's the team you'll build.\n\n\n\n\nLOCATION:\n\n - Onsite 4 days/week in San Francisco, CA\n\n\n\n\nWHY YOU'LL LOVE WORKING AT AIRBYTE:\n\nAt Airbyte, we believe great work happens when people feel supported, trusted, and empowered to grow. Our market-leading Total Rewards package is designed to help you thrive professionally and personally. Our benefits and perks include:\n\n\n\n• Flexible PTO with a culture that encourages at least 25 days off annually\n • 16 weeks fully paid parental leave for all parents\n • Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and dependents\n • 401(k) retirement plan\n • Professional development budget, conference sponsorship, and book reimbursement\n • Commuter benefits and monthly internet reimbursement\n\n •  Breakfast and lunch in our San Francisco office\n • A collaborative, in-person culture focused on learning, growth, and impact\n\n\n\nIf you find this role exciting, we encourage you to apply even if you think you don’t meet all of the requirements!\n\n\n\nWe are not accepting agency submissions or recruiting firm support for this role. Unsolicited resumes will not be considered.\n\n\n\nAirbyte is an equal opportunity employer that does not discriminate on the basis of actual or perceived race, creed, color, religion, national origin, ancestry, age, physical or mental disability, pregnancy, genetic information, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, marital status, familial status, domestic violence victim status, veteran or military status, or any other legally recognized protected basis under federal, state or local laws. Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.\n\n\n\nAirbyte is committed to providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities in our job application procedures. Please let us know if you need assistance or accommodations due to a disability."},{"id":"b59bbc91-fb77-4a08-9c47-0fca7f755942","title":"Senior Backend Engineer, Agent Infrastructure","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-10-12T20:53:02.796+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/airbyte/b59bbc91-fb77-4a08-9c47-0fca7f755942","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/airbyte/b59bbc91-fb77-4a08-9c47-0fca7f755942/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Airbyte is the data and action layer for AI agents. We give agents fast, accurate, authenticated access to business data across hundreds of sources, so they can discover the entities that matter, reason over real-time context, and take action in the systems they read from, not just observe them.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We started as the open-source standard for data movement and proved the economics of data integration at scale: hundreds of connectors, thousands of companies, and, since 2020, have raised $181M from leading investors including Benchmark, Accel, Altimeter, Coatue, and Y Combinator. As our CEO Michel Tricot puts it, \"the last ten years were all about structured data. The future is all about context.\" We're now building that context infrastructure for production-grade agents on the same open foundation, as agents become the primary consumers of enterprise data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our mission is unchanged: make data available and actionable to everyone, everywhere. That everyone now includes AI agents.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>The Role:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Airbyte is building the runtime that powers production-grade AI agents.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is not an ML research or prompt engineering role. We’re looking for an experienced backend or platform engineer who has built complex production systems and has also worked hands-on with AI agents, orchestration, retrieval, or LLM-powered applications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our AI Runtime sits between language models and the enterprise systems agents need to understand and act on. It is responsible for assembling the right context, identifying entities across systems, selecting tools and connectors, coordinating execution, validating evidence, enforcing permissions, and handling failures safely.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A user may ask something simple like:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">“Investigate this customer and tell me what changed.”</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Behind that request, the runtime may need to identify the customer across multiple systems, retrieve fresh data, determine which tools to call, coordinate multiple steps, validate the result, and return an answer with evidence the user can trust.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">That infrastructure is what you’ll help build.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re still early. The architecture is taking shape, but there is significant room to influence how the runtime is designed, how developers interact with it, and how we make agentic systems reliable in production.</p><h2><br /></h2><h2><strong>What You’ll Do:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build the Runtime</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and implement the orchestration layer that turns natural-language intent into reliable, multi-step execution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build systems for routing, state management, retries, failure handling, and long-running agent workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop systems for entity resolution, context assembly, connector orchestration, and evidence retrieval.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build reusable Skills that encapsulate business workflows and domain-specific capabilities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate connectors, APIs, tools, deterministic logic, retrieval systems, and multiple language models.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build Reliable AI Infrastructure</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design systems that retrieve and assemble the right enterprise context at runtime.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build evidence-backed reasoning with citations and traceability that users can inspect and verify.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Implement permission models, freshness validation, and action policies for production environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build evaluation, replay, observability, and debugging systems that help us understand why agents succeed or fail.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve the reliability of systems where model outputs may be probabilistic, but execution cannot be.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own Products End to End</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Take ambiguous product ideas from prototype through production.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own features across architecture, implementation, rollout, and iteration.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work directly with Product, Design, Sales Engineering, Customer Success, and customers to understand real-world problems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Write high-leverage code that creates reusable infrastructure for future product areas.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experiment with new agent architectures while maintaining production-grade reliability.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>What You’ll Need:</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You may be a strong fit if you are fundamentally a backend or platform engineer who has also spent meaningful time building production AI systems.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ years of software engineering experience building and operating production systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong backend engineering fundamentals and experience designing distributed systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building complex systems involving APIs, asynchronous workflows, concurrency, queues, state, retries, or distributed execution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience building production applications using LLMs, agents, RAG, tool calling, MCP, or similar technologies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with orchestration systems, workflow engines, developer platforms, or infrastructure products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong system design skills and the ability to reason about reliability, scale, observability, and failure modes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to move quickly from prototype to production without sacrificing engineering quality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong product instincts and comfort operating in ambiguous, 0-to-1 environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional written communication skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A strong bias toward ownership and shipping.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Nice To Have</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building agent infrastructure, agent platforms, or evaluation systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with orchestration technologies such as LangGraph, Temporal, MCP, or similar.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with retrieval systems, vector search, search infrastructure, or knowledge graphs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building developer tools or platform infrastructure.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with data infrastructure such as Kafka, Iceberg, Postgres, Spark, or modern data warehouses.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working on early-stage products where you helped define architecture and technical direction.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>What Success Looks Like</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Success is not measured by the sophistication of the prompts. It is measured by whether the runtime becomes more reliable, observable, and trustworthy over time.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ll build systems that:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assemble the right context and choose the correct connectors, tools, and Skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Execute multi-step workflows reliably.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Recover gracefully when something fails.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Produce evidence-backed answers with citations and traceability.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enforce permissions, freshness guarantees, and action policies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Learn from failures through replay, evaluation, and observability.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Allow users to focus on outcomes rather than coordinating individual tools themselves.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As the runtime evolves, developers and users should need to think less about the underlying tools and more about what they want to accomplish. The runtime should handle the complexity underneath.</p><h2><br /></h2><h2>Why This Role Matters</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">AI agents work impressively in demos. Making them reliable in production is much harder.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The difficult problems are often not the model itself. They are retrieving the right context, connecting to real enterprise systems, maintaining permissions, coordinating multiple actions, recovering from failures, and determining whether an answer can actually be trusted.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Airbyte already connects to hundreds of business systems. We’re building the runtime that allows agents to use that infrastructure intelligently and safely.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If we succeed, developers will not need to rebuild orchestration, retrieval, permissions, evaluation, and enterprise connectivity every time they build a new agent.</p><h2><br /></h2><h2>Location</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Onsite 4 days/week in San Francisco, CA</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Why You'll Love Working at Airbyte:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Airbyte, we believe great work happens when people feel supported, trusted, and empowered to grow. Our market-leading Total Rewards package is designed to help you thrive professionally and personally. Our benefits and perks include:</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Flexible PTO with a culture that encourages at least 25 days off annually<br /> • 16 weeks fully paid parental leave for all parents<br /> • Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and dependents<br /> • 401(k) retirement plan<br /> • Professional development budget, conference sponsorship, and book reimbursement<br /> • Commuter benefits and monthly internet reimbursement</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> •  Breakfast and lunch in our San Francisco office<br /> • A collaborative, in-person culture focused on learning, growth, and impact</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you find this role exciting, we encourage you to apply even if you think you don’t meet all of the requirements!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are not accepting agency submissions or recruiting firm support for this role. Unsolicited resumes will not be considered.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Airbyte is an equal opportunity employer that does not discriminate on the basis of actual or perceived race, creed, color, religion, national origin, ancestry, age, physical or mental disability, pregnancy, genetic information, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, marital status, familial status, domestic violence victim status, veteran or military status, or any other legally recognized protected basis under federal, state or local laws. Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Airbyte is committed to providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities in our job application procedures. Please let us know if you need assistance or accommodations due to a disability.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Airbyte is the data and action layer for AI agents. We give agents fast, accurate, authenticated access to business data across hundreds of sources, so they can discover the entities that matter, reason over real-time context, and take action in the systems they read from, not just observe them.\n\n\n\nWe started as the open-source standard for data movement and proved the economics of data integration at scale: hundreds of connectors, thousands of companies, and, since 2020, have raised $181M from leading investors including Benchmark, Accel, Altimeter, Coatue, and Y Combinator. As our CEO Michel Tricot puts it, \"the last ten years were all about structured data. The future is all about context.\" We're now building that context infrastructure for production-grade agents on the same open foundation, as agents become the primary consumers of enterprise data.\n\n\n\nOur mission is unchanged: make data available and actionable to everyone, everywhere. That everyone now includes AI agents.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE:\n\nAirbyte is building the runtime that powers production-grade AI agents.\n\n\n\nThis is not an ML research or prompt engineering role. We’re looking for an experienced backend or platform engineer who has built complex production systems and has also worked hands-on with AI agents, orchestration, retrieval, or LLM-powered applications.\n\n\n\nOur AI Runtime sits between language models and the enterprise systems agents need to understand and act on. It is responsible for assembling the right context, identifying entities across systems, selecting tools and connectors, coordinating execution, validating evidence, enforcing permissions, and handling failures safely.\n\n\n\nA user may ask something simple like:\n\n - “Investigate this customer and tell me what changed.”\n\nBehind that request, the runtime may need to identify the customer across multiple systems, retrieve fresh data, determine which tools to call, coordinate multiple steps, validate the result, and return an answer with evidence the user can trust.\n\n\n\nThat infrastructure is what you’ll help build.\n\n\n\nWe’re still early. The architecture is taking shape, but there is significant room to influence how the runtime is designed, how developers interact with it, and how we make agentic systems reliable in production.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO:\n\nBuild the Runtime\n\n - Design and implement the orchestration layer that turns natural-language intent into reliable, multi-step execution.\n\n - Build systems for routing, state management, retries, failure handling, and long-running agent workflows.\n\n - Develop systems for entity resolution, context assembly, connector orchestration, and evidence retrieval.\n\n - Build reusable Skills that encapsulate business workflows and domain-specific capabilities.\n\n - Coordinate connectors, APIs, tools, deterministic logic, retrieval systems, and multiple language models.\n\n\n\nBuild Reliable AI Infrastructure\n\n - Design systems that retrieve and assemble the right enterprise context at runtime.\n\n - Build evidence-backed reasoning with citations and traceability that users can inspect and verify.\n\n - Implement permission models, freshness validation, and action policies for production environments.\n\n - Build evaluation, replay, observability, and debugging systems that help us understand why agents succeed or fail.\n\n - Improve the reliability of systems where model outputs may be probabilistic, but execution cannot be.\n\n\n\nOwn Products End to End\n\n - Take ambiguous product ideas from prototype through production.\n\n - Own features across architecture, implementation, rollout, and iteration.\n\n - Work directly with Product, Design, Sales Engineering, Customer Success, and customers to understand real-world problems.\n\n - Write high-leverage code that creates reusable infrastructure for future product areas.\n\n - Experiment with new agent architectures while maintaining production-grade reliability.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL NEED:\n\nYou may be a strong fit if you are fundamentally a backend or platform engineer who has also spent meaningful time building production AI systems.\n\n - 7+ years of software engineering experience building and operating production systems.\n\n - Strong backend engineering fundamentals and experience designing distributed systems.\n\n - Experience building complex systems involving APIs, asynchronous workflows, concurrency, queues, state, retries, or distributed execution.\n\n - Hands-on experience building production applications using LLMs, agents, RAG, tool calling, MCP, or similar technologies.\n\n - Experience with orchestration systems, workflow engines, developer platforms, or infrastructure products.\n\n - Strong system design skills and the ability to reason about reliability, scale, observability, and failure modes.\n\n - Ability to move quickly from prototype to production without sacrificing engineering quality.\n\n - Strong product instincts and comfort operating in ambiguous, 0-to-1 environments.\n\n - Exceptional written communication skills.\n\n - A strong bias toward ownership and shipping.\n\n\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience building agent infrastructure, agent platforms, or evaluation systems.\n\n - Familiarity with orchestration technologies such as LangGraph, Temporal, MCP, or similar.\n\n - Experience with retrieval systems, vector search, search infrastructure, or knowledge graphs.\n\n - Experience building developer tools or platform infrastructure.\n\n - Experience with data infrastructure such as Kafka, Iceberg, Postgres, Spark, or modern data warehouses.\n\n - Experience working on early-stage products where you helped define architecture and technical direction.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT SUCCESS LOOKS LIKE\n\nSuccess is not measured by the sophistication of the prompts. It is measured by whether the runtime becomes more reliable, observable, and trustworthy over time.\n\nYou’ll build systems that:\n\n - Assemble the right context and choose the correct connectors, tools, and Skills.\n\n - Execute multi-step workflows reliably.\n\n - Recover gracefully when something fails.\n\n - Produce evidence-backed answers with citations and traceability.\n\n - Enforce permissions, freshness guarantees, and action policies.\n\n - Learn from failures through replay, evaluation, and observability.\n\n - Allow users to focus on outcomes rather than coordinating individual tools themselves.\n\nAs the runtime evolves, developers and users should need to think less about the underlying tools and more about what they want to accomplish. The runtime should handle the complexity underneath.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHY THIS ROLE MATTERS\n\nAI agents work impressively in demos. Making them reliable in production is much harder.\n\nThe difficult problems are often not the model itself. They are retrieving the right context, connecting to real enterprise systems, maintaining permissions, coordinating multiple actions, recovering from failures, and determining whether an answer can actually be trusted.\n\nAirbyte already connects to hundreds of business systems. We’re building the runtime that allows agents to use that infrastructure intelligently and safely.\n\nIf we succeed, developers will not need to rebuild orchestration, retrieval, permissions, evaluation, and enterprise connectivity every time they build a new agent.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nLOCATION\n\n - Onsite 4 days/week in San Francisco, CA\n\n\n\n\nWHY YOU'LL LOVE WORKING AT AIRBYTE:\n\nAt Airbyte, we believe great work happens when people feel supported, trusted, and empowered to grow. Our market-leading Total Rewards package is designed to help you thrive professionally and personally. Our benefits and perks include:\n\n\n\n• Flexible PTO with a culture that encourages at least 25 days off annually\n • 16 weeks fully paid parental leave for all parents\n • Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and dependents\n • 401(k) retirement plan\n • Professional development budget, conference sponsorship, and book reimbursement\n • Commuter benefits and monthly internet reimbursement\n\n •  Breakfast and lunch in our San Francisco office\n • A collaborative, in-person culture focused on learning, growth, and impact\n\n\n\nIf you find this role exciting, we encourage you to apply even if you think you don’t meet all of the requirements!\n\n\n\nWe are not accepting agency submissions or recruiting firm support for this role. Unsolicited resumes will not be considered.\n\n\n\nAirbyte is an equal opportunity employer that does not discriminate on the basis of actual or perceived race, creed, color, religion, national origin, ancestry, age, physical or mental disability, pregnancy, genetic information, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, marital status, familial status, domestic violence victim status, veteran or military status, or any other legally recognized protected basis under federal, state or local laws. Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.\n\n\n\nAirbyte is committed to providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities in our job application procedures. Please let us know if you need assistance or accommodations due to a disability."},{"id":"735d5deb-ba6e-49b2-88ba-5ebdf8d315a0","title":"Senior Software Engineer, Platform Fullstack","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-10-17T02:12:12.543+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/airbyte/735d5deb-ba6e-49b2-88ba-5ebdf8d315a0","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/airbyte/735d5deb-ba6e-49b2-88ba-5ebdf8d315a0/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Airbyte is the data and action layer for AI agents. We give agents fast, accurate, authenticated access to business data across hundreds of sources, so they can discover the entities that matter, reason over real-time context, and take action in the systems they read from, not just observe them.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We started as the open-source standard for data movement and proved the economics of data integration at scale: hundreds of connectors, thousands of companies, and, since 2020, have raised $181M from leading investors including Benchmark, Accel, Altimeter, Coatue, and Y Combinator. As our CEO Michel Tricot puts it, \"the last ten years were all about structured data. The future is all about context.\" We're now building that context infrastructure for production-grade agents on the same open foundation, as agents become the primary consumers of enterprise data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our mission is unchanged: make data available and actionable to everyone, everywhere. That everyone now includes AI agents.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>The Role:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Every great product is built on a great platform. At Airbyte, the Platform team builds the systems that power every product we ship, including Airbyte Cloud, Airbyte Flex, and Airbyte Agents.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We create the infrastructure, internal tooling, developer platforms, and user-facing product surfaces that allow engineers to build quickly, deploy safely, and operate reliably at scale. Our work spans cloud infrastructure, deployment automation, observability, engineering productivity, and the product experiences that our customers and engineers rely on every day.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Senior Fullstack Engineer on Platform, you'll work across the full stack to build both the internal tools that accelerate engineering and the user-facing features that customers interact with directly. You'll move fluidly between building an internal deployment dashboard and shipping a product feature in Airbyte Cloud.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is ideal for engineers who care about craft across the entire stack, whether the user is an internal engineer or an external customer, and who believe great platform work makes everything around it better.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h2><strong>What You’ll Do:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build Internal Platform Products</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and build applications that power Airbyte's engineering platform and product surfaces.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop internal dashboards for deployments, infrastructure health, connector operations, and platform performance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and improve user-facing features in Airbyte Cloud and Flex, working closely with product and design.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create self-service tools that enable engineers to provision infrastructure, manage services, and troubleshoot production systems.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build Across the Stack</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build modern React and TypeScript applications backed by scalable backend services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design APIs and services that support both internal engineering workflows and customer-facing product features.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with Platform Engineers, SREs, Product Engineering, Product Managers, and Designers to ship high-quality software.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve the usability and reliability of the systems that power Airbyte's products, for both internal and external users.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Improve Developer Experience</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build tooling that automates repetitive engineering work and reduces friction across the org.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve release workflows, deployment visibility, and operational dashboards.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to the quality of user-facing product surfaces: performance, accessibility, and reliability.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help establish engineering standards and reusable platform components.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive Operational Excellence</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build interfaces that improve observability, incident response, and production operations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create tools that help engineers and customers understand system health, deployment status, and service reliability.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve visibility into platform performance through dashboards, metrics, and reporting.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Continuously identify opportunities to reduce operational toil through automation.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Technical Leadership</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mentor engineers through design reviews, architecture discussions, and technical leadership.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Raise the quality bar for frontend architecture, testing, accessibility, and maintainability.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to platform-wide engineering standards and best practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help shape the future of Airbyte's platform and product engineering.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h2><strong>What You’ll Need:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ years of experience building production fullstack applications.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep expertise with React and TypeScript.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong backend engineering experience building APIs and distributed systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience shipping user-facing SaaS products alongside internal tools, developer platforms, or operational dashboards.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with product managers and designers to ship customer-facing features.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with cloud infrastructure and modern deployment workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong product instincts and customer empathy, whether your user is an engineer or an external customer.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written and verbal communication skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A bias toward ownership, automation, and shipping.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Nice To Have:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Kubernetes, Docker, Terraform, or cloud infrastructure.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with GitHub Actions, CI/CD pipelines, or developer productivity tooling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with observability platforms such as Grafana, Datadog, or Prometheus.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Java or Kotlin.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with distributed systems and cloud-native architectures.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building internal engineering tools or developer platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with data infrastructure or large-scale SaaS platforms.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What Success Looks Like:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Success means the software you build makes both engineers and customers more effective.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Engineers deploy with confidence.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Infrastructure is easier to understand.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Production issues are easier to diagnose.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Operational workflows become self-service.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Development becomes faster, safer, and more reliable.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll build software that spans the full spectrum, from internal platforms that multiply engineering velocity to product features that customers use every day.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Why This Role Matters:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Platform Engineering is the foundation beneath Airbyte Cloud, Airbyte Flex, and Airbyte Agents. Our mission is to build the infrastructure, tooling, and developer experience that allows every engineering team to deliver reliable software at scale.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">When Platform succeeds, engineers move faster and customers get a better product. You'll help build the systems that let Airbyte focus on what matters most: building the future of data movement and AI.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h2><strong>Location:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Onsite 4 days/week in San Francisco, CA</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Why You'll Love Working at Airbyte:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Airbyte, we believe great work happens when people feel supported, trusted, and empowered to grow. Our market-leading Total Rewards package is designed to help you thrive professionally and personally. Our benefits and perks include:</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Flexible PTO with a culture that encourages at least 25 days off annually<br /> • 16 weeks fully paid parental leave for all parents<br /> • Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and dependents<br /> • 401(k) retirement plan<br /> • Professional development budget, conference sponsorship, and book reimbursement<br /> • Commuter benefits and monthly internet reimbursement</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> •  Breakfast and lunch in our San Francisco office<br /> • A collaborative, in-person culture focused on learning, growth, and impact</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you find this role exciting, we encourage you to apply even if you think you don’t meet all of the requirements!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are not accepting agency submissions or recruiting firm support for this role. Unsolicited resumes will not be considered.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Airbyte is an equal opportunity employer that does not discriminate on the basis of actual or perceived race, creed, color, religion, national origin, ancestry, age, physical or mental disability, pregnancy, genetic information, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, marital status, familial status, domestic violence victim status, veteran or military status, or any other legally recognized protected basis under federal, state or local laws. Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Airbyte is committed to providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities in our job application procedures. Please let us know if you need assistance or accommodations due to a disability.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Airbyte is the data and action layer for AI agents. We give agents fast, accurate, authenticated access to business data across hundreds of sources, so they can discover the entities that matter, reason over real-time context, and take action in the systems they read from, not just observe them.\n\n\n\nWe started as the open-source standard for data movement and proved the economics of data integration at scale: hundreds of connectors, thousands of companies, and, since 2020, have raised $181M from leading investors including Benchmark, Accel, Altimeter, Coatue, and Y Combinator. As our CEO Michel Tricot puts it, \"the last ten years were all about structured data. The future is all about context.\" We're now building that context infrastructure for production-grade agents on the same open foundation, as agents become the primary consumers of enterprise data.\n\n\n\nOur mission is unchanged: make data available and actionable to everyone, everywhere. That everyone now includes AI agents.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE:\n\nEvery great product is built on a great platform. At Airbyte, the Platform team builds the systems that power every product we ship, including Airbyte Cloud, Airbyte Flex, and Airbyte Agents.\n\n\n\nWe create the infrastructure, internal tooling, developer platforms, and user-facing product surfaces that allow engineers to build quickly, deploy safely, and operate reliably at scale. Our work spans cloud infrastructure, deployment automation, observability, engineering productivity, and the product experiences that our customers and engineers rely on every day.\n\n\n\nAs a Senior Fullstack Engineer on Platform, you'll work across the full stack to build both the internal tools that accelerate engineering and the user-facing features that customers interact with directly. You'll move fluidly between building an internal deployment dashboard and shipping a product feature in Airbyte Cloud.\n\n\n\nThis role is ideal for engineers who care about craft across the entire stack, whether the user is an internal engineer or an external customer, and who believe great platform work makes everything around it better.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO:\n\n\n\nBuild Internal Platform Products\n\n - Design and build applications that power Airbyte's engineering platform and product surfaces.\n\n - Develop internal dashboards for deployments, infrastructure health, connector operations, and platform performance.\n\n - Build and improve user-facing features in Airbyte Cloud and Flex, working closely with product and design.\n\n - Create self-service tools that enable engineers to provision infrastructure, manage services, and troubleshoot production systems.\n\n\n\nBuild Across the Stack\n\n - Build modern React and TypeScript applications backed by scalable backend services.\n\n - Design APIs and services that support both internal engineering workflows and customer-facing product features.\n\n - Collaborate with Platform Engineers, SREs, Product Engineering, Product Managers, and Designers to ship high-quality software.\n\n - Improve the usability and reliability of the systems that power Airbyte's products, for both internal and external users.\n\n\n\nImprove Developer Experience\n\n - Build tooling that automates repetitive engineering work and reduces friction across the org.\n\n - Improve release workflows, deployment visibility, and operational dashboards.\n\n - Contribute to the quality of user-facing product surfaces: performance, accessibility, and reliability.\n\n - Help establish engineering standards and reusable platform components.\n\n\n\nDrive Operational Excellence\n\n - Build interfaces that improve observability, incident response, and production operations.\n\n - Create tools that help engineers and customers understand system health, deployment status, and service reliability.\n\n - Improve visibility into platform performance through dashboards, metrics, and reporting.\n\n - Continuously identify opportunities to reduce operational toil through automation.\n\n\n\nTechnical Leadership\n\n - Mentor engineers through design reviews, architecture discussions, and technical leadership.\n\n - Raise the quality bar for frontend architecture, testing, accessibility, and maintainability.\n\n - Contribute to platform-wide engineering standards and best practices.\n\n - Help shape the future of Airbyte's platform and product engineering.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL NEED:\n\n - 7+ years of experience building production fullstack applications.\n\n - Deep expertise with React and TypeScript.\n\n - Strong backend engineering experience building APIs and distributed systems.\n\n - Experience shipping user-facing SaaS products alongside internal tools, developer platforms, or operational dashboards.\n\n - Experience working with product managers and designers to ship customer-facing features.\n\n - Familiarity with cloud infrastructure and modern deployment workflows.\n\n - Strong product instincts and customer empathy, whether your user is an engineer or an external customer.\n\n - Excellent written and verbal communication skills.\n\n - A bias toward ownership, automation, and shipping.\n\n\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE:\n\n - Experience with Kubernetes, Docker, Terraform, or cloud infrastructure.\n\n - Experience with GitHub Actions, CI/CD pipelines, or developer productivity tooling.\n\n - Familiarity with observability platforms such as Grafana, Datadog, or Prometheus.\n\n - Experience with Java or Kotlin.\n\n - Experience with distributed systems and cloud-native architectures.\n\n - Experience building internal engineering tools or developer platforms.\n\n - Familiarity with data infrastructure or large-scale SaaS platforms.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT SUCCESS LOOKS LIKE:\n\nSuccess means the software you build makes both engineers and customers more effective.\n\nEngineers deploy with confidence.\n\nInfrastructure is easier to understand.\n\nProduction issues are easier to diagnose.\n\nOperational workflows become self-service.\n\nDevelopment becomes faster, safer, and more reliable.\n\nYou'll build software that spans the full spectrum, from internal platforms that multiply engineering velocity to product features that customers use every day.\n\n\n\n\nWHY THIS ROLE MATTERS:\n\nPlatform Engineering is the foundation beneath Airbyte Cloud, Airbyte Flex, and Airbyte Agents. Our mission is to build the infrastructure, tooling, and developer experience that allows every engineering team to deliver reliable software at scale.\n\n\n\nWhen Platform succeeds, engineers move faster and customers get a better product. You'll help build the systems that let Airbyte focus on what matters most: building the future of data movement and AI.\n\n \n\n\nLOCATION:\n\n - Onsite 4 days/week in San Francisco, CA\n\n\n\n\nWHY YOU'LL LOVE WORKING AT AIRBYTE:\n\nAt Airbyte, we believe great work happens when people feel supported, trusted, and empowered to grow. Our market-leading Total Rewards package is designed to help you thrive professionally and personally. Our benefits and perks include:\n\n\n\n• Flexible PTO with a culture that encourages at least 25 days off annually\n • 16 weeks fully paid parental leave for all parents\n • Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and dependents\n • 401(k) retirement plan\n • Professional development budget, conference sponsorship, and book reimbursement\n • Commuter benefits and monthly internet reimbursement\n\n •  Breakfast and lunch in our San Francisco office\n • A collaborative, in-person culture focused on learning, growth, and impact\n\n\n\nIf you find this role exciting, we encourage you to apply even if you think you don’t meet all of the requirements!\n\n\n\nWe are not accepting agency submissions or recruiting firm support for this role. Unsolicited resumes will not be considered.\n\n\n\nAirbyte is an equal opportunity employer that does not discriminate on the basis of actual or perceived race, creed, color, religion, national origin, ancestry, age, physical or mental disability, pregnancy, genetic information, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, marital status, familial status, domestic violence victim status, veteran or military status, or any other legally recognized protected basis under federal, state or local laws. Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.\n\n\n\nAirbyte is committed to providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities in our job application procedures. Please let us know if you need assistance or accommodations due to a disability."},{"id":"5930fed9-c4f6-43c3-87be-3402c2c46489","title":"Senior Site Reliability Engineer","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-10-16T21:58:35.252+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/airbyte/5930fed9-c4f6-43c3-87be-3402c2c46489","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/airbyte/5930fed9-c4f6-43c3-87be-3402c2c46489/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Airbyte is the data and action layer for AI agents. We give agents fast, accurate, authenticated access to business data across hundreds of sources, so they can discover the entities that matter, reason over real-time context, and take action in the systems they read from, not just observe them.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We started as the open-source standard for data movement and proved the economics of data integration at scale: hundreds of connectors, thousands of companies, and, since 2020, have raised $181M from leading investors including Benchmark, Accel, Altimeter, Coatue, and Y Combinator. As our CEO Michel Tricot puts it, \"the last ten years were all about structured data. The future is all about context.\" We're now building that context infrastructure for production-grade agents on the same open foundation, as agents become the primary consumers of enterprise data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our mission is unchanged: make data available and actionable to everyone, everywhere. That everyone now includes AI agents.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h2><strong>The Role:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll be one of two infrastructure and reliability specialists on the Data Replication team, a full-stack product team running millions of sync jobs a week that power thousands of data use cases across multiple regions and clouds. You'll build and maintain the infrastructure, set reliability standards, drive down incidents, and make it easier and safer for engineers to ship. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Expect to spend roughly 30 to 50% of your time in backend application code, and the rest on infrastructure and reliability. When the fix belongs in the application, you'll ship it there yourself, and you'll build features alongside product engineers. We believe every abstraction leaks, so the best engineers work up and down the stack. You're equally comfortable in a Terraform file, a Kubernetes cluster, a service's codebase, and a postmortem doc. And with two of you in the room, we want someone who will challenge a design, not just implement it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We expect engineers here to actively use AI as a force multiplier: agentic tools to automate toil, augment incident response, and build smarter internal tooling. If you're not already doing this, you should be excited to start. We care as much about how you work as what you build. Trust, directness, and craftsmanship matter here.</p><h2></h2><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h2><strong>What You’ll Do:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the infrastructure underpinning the Data Replication platform: Kubernetes clusters, CI/CD pipelines, secrets management, networking, and cloud resource configuration across AWS and GCP.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work across the stack: ship backend features and fixes in application code alongside product engineers, not just the infrastructure underneath them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve performance and efficiency at scale, from bursty job scheduling to right-sizing compute.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help us ship safely into customer-managed environments, where Airbyte runs in infrastructure we don't control.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evolve observability, alerting, and anomaly detection, with an eye toward LLM automation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build AI-augmented release and internal tooling: canary deployments, progressive rollouts, automated release qualification, and rollback automation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set the infrastructure bar for the team: build self-serve tooling, write runbooks, and coach engineers to own more of their stack.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What You’ll Need:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ years in infrastructure, platform engineering, SRE, or DevOps.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on ownership of Kubernetes, Helm, and Terraform in production environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep experience with observability stacks (Prometheus, Grafana, Datadog) and on-call operations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with CI/CD pipeline ownership and developer tooling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience shipping changes to backend services in [language], not only infrastructure code, and the appetite to do more of it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong design judgment, and the confidence to challenge infrastructure decisions with data.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency with AI tools: LLMs and agentic frameworks to automate, debug faster, and reduce toil.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A startup-ready mindset: comfortable with ambiguity, moving fast, and owning problems end to end.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h2><strong>Nice To Have:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Data pipelines, replication systems, or ETL/ELT platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Control plane / data plane architectures or internal developer platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Shipping software customers run in their own environments (Helm charts, upgrade paths, varied configurations).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Airbyte, CDKs, or connector-based architectures.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Location:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Onsite 4 days/week in San Francisco, CA</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Why You'll Love Working at Airbyte:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Airbyte, we believe great work happens when people feel supported, trusted, and empowered to grow. Our market-leading Total Rewards package is designed to help you thrive professionally and personally. Our benefits and perks include:</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Flexible PTO with a culture that encourages at least 25 days off annually<br /> • 16 weeks fully paid parental leave for all parents<br /> • Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and dependents<br /> • 401(k) retirement plan<br /> • Professional development budget, conference sponsorship, and book reimbursement<br /> • Commuter benefits and monthly internet reimbursement</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> •  Breakfast and lunch in our San Francisco office<br /> • A collaborative, in-person culture focused on learning, growth, and impact</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you find this role exciting, we encourage you to apply even if you think you don’t meet all of the requirements!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are not accepting agency submissions or recruiting firm support for this role. Unsolicited resumes will not be considered.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Airbyte is an equal opportunity employer that does not discriminate on the basis of actual or perceived race, creed, color, religion, national origin, ancestry, age, physical or mental disability, pregnancy, genetic information, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, marital status, familial status, domestic violence victim status, veteran or military status, or any other legally recognized protected basis under federal, state or local laws. Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Airbyte is committed to providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities in our job application procedures. Please let us know if you need assistance or accommodations due to a disability.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Airbyte is the data and action layer for AI agents. We give agents fast, accurate, authenticated access to business data across hundreds of sources, so they can discover the entities that matter, reason over real-time context, and take action in the systems they read from, not just observe them.\n\n\n\nWe started as the open-source standard for data movement and proved the economics of data integration at scale: hundreds of connectors, thousands of companies, and, since 2020, have raised $181M from leading investors including Benchmark, Accel, Altimeter, Coatue, and Y Combinator. As our CEO Michel Tricot puts it, \"the last ten years were all about structured data. The future is all about context.\" We're now building that context infrastructure for production-grade agents on the same open foundation, as agents become the primary consumers of enterprise data.\n\n\n\nOur mission is unchanged: make data available and actionable to everyone, everywhere. That everyone now includes AI agents.\n\n\n\n \n\n\nTHE ROLE:\n\nYou'll be one of two infrastructure and reliability specialists on the Data Replication team, a full-stack product team running millions of sync jobs a week that power thousands of data use cases across multiple regions and clouds. You'll build and maintain the infrastructure, set reliability standards, drive down incidents, and make it easier and safer for engineers to ship. \n\nExpect to spend roughly 30 to 50% of your time in backend application code, and the rest on infrastructure and reliability. When the fix belongs in the application, you'll ship it there yourself, and you'll build features alongside product engineers. We believe every abstraction leaks, so the best engineers work up and down the stack. You're equally comfortable in a Terraform file, a Kubernetes cluster, a service's codebase, and a postmortem doc. And with two of you in the room, we want someone who will challenge a design, not just implement it.\n\nWe expect engineers here to actively use AI as a force multiplier: agentic tools to automate toil, augment incident response, and build smarter internal tooling. If you're not already doing this, you should be excited to start. We care as much about how you work as what you build. Trust, directness, and craftsmanship matter here.\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO:\n\n - Own the infrastructure underpinning the Data Replication platform: Kubernetes clusters, CI/CD pipelines, secrets management, networking, and cloud resource configuration across AWS and GCP.\n\n - Work across the stack: ship backend features and fixes in application code alongside product engineers, not just the infrastructure underneath them.\n\n - Improve performance and efficiency at scale, from bursty job scheduling to right-sizing compute.\n\n - Help us ship safely into customer-managed environments, where Airbyte runs in infrastructure we don't control.\n\n - Evolve observability, alerting, and anomaly detection, with an eye toward LLM automation.\n\n - Build AI-augmented release and internal tooling: canary deployments, progressive rollouts, automated release qualification, and rollback automation.\n\n - Set the infrastructure bar for the team: build self-serve tooling, write runbooks, and coach engineers to own more of their stack.\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL NEED:\n\n - 7+ years in infrastructure, platform engineering, SRE, or DevOps.\n\n - Hands-on ownership of Kubernetes, Helm, and Terraform in production environments.\n\n - Deep experience with observability stacks (Prometheus, Grafana, Datadog) and on-call operations.\n\n - Experience with CI/CD pipeline ownership and developer tooling.\n\n - Experience shipping changes to backend services in [language], not only infrastructure code, and the appetite to do more of it.\n\n - Strong design judgment, and the confidence to challenge infrastructure decisions with data.\n\n - Fluency with AI tools: LLMs and agentic frameworks to automate, debug faster, and reduce toil.\n\n - A startup-ready mindset: comfortable with ambiguity, moving fast, and owning problems end to end.\n\n \n\n\nNICE TO HAVE:\n\n - Data pipelines, replication systems, or ETL/ELT platforms.\n\n - Control plane / data plane architectures or internal developer platforms.\n\n - Shipping software customers run in their own environments (Helm charts, upgrade paths, varied configurations).\n\n - Experience with Airbyte, CDKs, or connector-based architectures.\n\n\nLOCATION:\n\n - Onsite 4 days/week in San Francisco, CA\n\n\n\n\nWHY YOU'LL LOVE WORKING AT AIRBYTE:\n\nAt Airbyte, we believe great work happens when people feel supported, trusted, and empowered to grow. Our market-leading Total Rewards package is designed to help you thrive professionally and personally. Our benefits and perks include:\n\n\n\n• Flexible PTO with a culture that encourages at least 25 days off annually\n • 16 weeks fully paid parental leave for all parents\n • Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and dependents\n • 401(k) retirement plan\n • Professional development budget, conference sponsorship, and book reimbursement\n • Commuter benefits and monthly internet reimbursement\n\n •  Breakfast and lunch in our San Francisco office\n • A collaborative, in-person culture focused on learning, growth, and impact\n\n\n\nIf you find this role exciting, we encourage you to apply even if you think you don’t meet all of the requirements!\n\n\n\nWe are not accepting agency submissions or recruiting firm support for this role. Unsolicited resumes will not be considered.\n\n\n\nAirbyte is an equal opportunity employer that does not discriminate on the basis of actual or perceived race, creed, color, religion, national origin, ancestry, age, physical or mental disability, pregnancy, genetic information, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, marital status, familial status, domestic violence victim status, veteran or military status, or any other legally recognized protected basis under federal, state or local laws. Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.\n\n\n\nAirbyte is committed to providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities in our job application procedures. Please let us know if you need assistance or accommodations due to a disability."},{"id":"af867d0a-bd70-4a8e-80f9-13567bd0f3a8","title":"Accounting Manager","department":"Finance ","team":"Finance ","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"San Francisco","secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-10-16T20:55:22.484+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"San Francisco"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/airbyte/af867d0a-bd70-4a8e-80f9-13567bd0f3a8","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/airbyte/af867d0a-bd70-4a8e-80f9-13567bd0f3a8/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Airbyte is the data and action layer for AI agents. We give agents fast, accurate, authenticated access to business data across hundreds of sources, so they can discover the entities that matter, reason over real-time context, and take action in the systems they read from, not just observe them.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We started as the open-source standard for data movement and proved the economics of data integration at scale: hundreds of connectors, thousands of companies, and, since 2020, have raised $181M from leading investors including Benchmark, Accel, Altimeter, Coatue, and Y Combinator. As our CEO Michel Tricot puts it, \"the last ten years were all about structured data. The future is all about context.\" We're now building that context infrastructure for production-grade agents on the same open foundation, as agents become the primary consumers of enterprise data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our mission is unchanged: make data available and actionable to everyone, everywhere. That everyone now includes AI agents.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h2><strong>The Role:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Airbyte's Accounting Manager, you’ll own the day-to-day of our accounting operations and reporting - and you’ll help us rebuild how that work gets done, replacing manual processes and outsourced accounting firm dependencies with clean, automated, in-house workflows.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We currently run a lean model with an outsourced accounting firm and a Senior Accountant. You’ll manage both, and over time help us bring accounting back in-house - taking ownership of more of the function as you go. You’ll report directly to the Director of Finance (who reports to the COO) as a thought partner on automating our close and operations, and you’ll have real room to experiment with modern tooling and AI to do it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're hiring someone with the intention of investing in their long-term growth. As the business evolves, this role is expected to take on increasing ownership and responsibility, with the opportunity to help shape and ultimately lead the accounting function over time. If you want to build a modern accounting function - not just maintain one - this is that seat.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h2><strong>What You’ll Do:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own accounting operations and reporting - GL, AP/AR, and the general ledger close - with accuracy, timeliness, and US GAAP compliance; you’ll operate with high ownership and strong judgment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Run the month-end close, and continuously shorten and automate it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage a Senior Accountant and our outsourced accounting team, and help lead the transition of work in-house over time.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prepare for and support external audits, including documentation, technical accounting memos, and internal controls.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Apply and help maintain technical accounting policies, including revenue recognition under ASC 606 and lease accounting under ASC 842.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluate, implement, and optimize accounting systems and workflows - reducing manual work and building for scale.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner cross-functionally with Sales, Marketing, Engineering, and Support to keep accounting accurate across our business systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as a thought partner to the Director of Finance on automating close and operations, including using AI where it drives real impact.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grow into broader ownership of the accounting function as the business scales.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Perform and review detailed flux and variance analysis, identifying and proactively investigating unexpected trends or anomalies in our financials.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h2><strong>What You’ll Need:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of progressive accounting experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ideally a Big 4 audit and startup combined background.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of US GAAP, including revenue recognition (ASC 606) and lease accounting (ASC 842).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong systems instincts - you’ve evaluated, implemented, or redesigned accounting workflows and tools, and you reach for automation before manual effort.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Tech-savvy and genuinely AI-curious - you’ve explored (or are eager to explore) how automation and AI can transform accounting, and you like building.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">An operational, ownership mindset - pragmatic, solution-oriented, and able to work autonomously. Startups move fast, so the ability to adapt and learn quickly is key.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A people person. We have a strong culture and care about bringing in teammates who fit in and make it better.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h2><strong>Nice To Have:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">CPA or CMA certification is a plus.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience implementing or migrating to a new ERP system.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with PLG and/or enterprise SaaS revenue models.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with our stack: NetSuite, Rillet, Campfire, Ramp, Carta, Orb, and Claude Code.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with auditing.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h2><strong>Location:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Onsite 4 days/week in San Francisco, CA</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Why You'll Love Working at Airbyte:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Airbyte, we believe great work happens when people feel supported, trusted, and empowered to grow. Our market-leading Total Rewards package is designed to help you thrive professionally and personally. Our benefits and perks include:</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Flexible PTO with a culture that encourages at least 25 days off annually<br /> • 16 weeks fully paid parental leave for all parents<br /> • Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and dependents<br /> • 401(k) retirement plan<br /> • Professional development budget, conference sponsorship, and book reimbursement<br /> • Commuter benefits and monthly internet reimbursement</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> •  Breakfast and lunch in our San Francisco office<br /> • A collaborative, in-person culture focused on learning, growth, and impact</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you find this role exciting, we encourage you to apply even if you think you don’t meet all of the requirements!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are not accepting agency submissions or recruiting firm support for this role. Unsolicited resumes will not be considered.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Airbyte is an equal opportunity employer that does not discriminate on the basis of actual or perceived race, creed, color, religion, national origin, ancestry, age, physical or mental disability, pregnancy, genetic information, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, marital status, familial status, domestic violence victim status, veteran or military status, or any other legally recognized protected basis under federal, state or local laws. Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Airbyte is committed to providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities in our job application procedures. Please let us know if you need assistance or accommodations due to a disability.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Airbyte is the data and action layer for AI agents. We give agents fast, accurate, authenticated access to business data across hundreds of sources, so they can discover the entities that matter, reason over real-time context, and take action in the systems they read from, not just observe them.\n\n\n\nWe started as the open-source standard for data movement and proved the economics of data integration at scale: hundreds of connectors, thousands of companies, and, since 2020, have raised $181M from leading investors including Benchmark, Accel, Altimeter, Coatue, and Y Combinator. As our CEO Michel Tricot puts it, \"the last ten years were all about structured data. The future is all about context.\" We're now building that context infrastructure for production-grade agents on the same open foundation, as agents become the primary consumers of enterprise data.\n\n\n\nOur mission is unchanged: make data available and actionable to everyone, everywhere. That everyone now includes AI agents.\n\n \n\n\nTHE ROLE:\n\nAs Airbyte's Accounting Manager, you’ll own the day-to-day of our accounting operations and reporting - and you’ll help us rebuild how that work gets done, replacing manual processes and outsourced accounting firm dependencies with clean, automated, in-house workflows.\n\nWe currently run a lean model with an outsourced accounting firm and a Senior Accountant. You’ll manage both, and over time help us bring accounting back in-house - taking ownership of more of the function as you go. You’ll report directly to the Director of Finance (who reports to the COO) as a thought partner on automating our close and operations, and you’ll have real room to experiment with modern tooling and AI to do it.\n\nWe're hiring someone with the intention of investing in their long-term growth. As the business evolves, this role is expected to take on increasing ownership and responsibility, with the opportunity to help shape and ultimately lead the accounting function over time. If you want to build a modern accounting function - not just maintain one - this is that seat.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO:\n\n - Own accounting operations and reporting - GL, AP/AR, and the general ledger close - with accuracy, timeliness, and US GAAP compliance; you’ll operate with high ownership and strong judgment.\n\n - Run the month-end close, and continuously shorten and automate it.\n\n - Manage a Senior Accountant and our outsourced accounting team, and help lead the transition of work in-house over time.\n\n - Prepare for and support external audits, including documentation, technical accounting memos, and internal controls.\n\n - Apply and help maintain technical accounting policies, including revenue recognition under ASC 606 and lease accounting under ASC 842.\n\n - Evaluate, implement, and optimize accounting systems and workflows - reducing manual work and building for scale.\n\n - Partner cross-functionally with Sales, Marketing, Engineering, and Support to keep accounting accurate across our business systems.\n\n - Act as a thought partner to the Director of Finance on automating close and operations, including using AI where it drives real impact.\n\n - Grow into broader ownership of the accounting function as the business scales.\n\n - Perform and review detailed flux and variance analysis, identifying and proactively investigating unexpected trends or anomalies in our financials.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL NEED:\n\n - 5+ years of progressive accounting experience.\n\n - Ideally a Big 4 audit and startup combined background.\n\n - Working knowledge of US GAAP, including revenue recognition (ASC 606) and lease accounting (ASC 842).\n\n - Strong systems instincts - you’ve evaluated, implemented, or redesigned accounting workflows and tools, and you reach for automation before manual effort.\n\n - Tech-savvy and genuinely AI-curious - you’ve explored (or are eager to explore) how automation and AI can transform accounting, and you like building.\n\n - An operational, ownership mindset - pragmatic, solution-oriented, and able to work autonomously. Startups move fast, so the ability to adapt and learn quickly is key.\n\n - A people person. We have a strong culture and care about bringing in teammates who fit in and make it better.\n\n \n\n\nNICE TO HAVE:\n\n - CPA or CMA certification is a plus.\n\n - Experience implementing or migrating to a new ERP system.\n\n - Experience with PLG and/or enterprise SaaS revenue models.\n\n - Familiarity with our stack: NetSuite, Rillet, Campfire, Ramp, Carta, Orb, and Claude Code.\n\n - Experience with auditing.\n\n \n\n\nLOCATION:\n\n - Onsite 4 days/week in San Francisco, CA\n\n\n\n\nWHY YOU'LL LOVE WORKING AT AIRBYTE:\n\nAt Airbyte, we believe great work happens when people feel supported, trusted, and empowered to grow. Our market-leading Total Rewards package is designed to help you thrive professionally and personally. Our benefits and perks include:\n\n\n\n• Flexible PTO with a culture that encourages at least 25 days off annually\n • 16 weeks fully paid parental leave for all parents\n • Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and dependents\n • 401(k) retirement plan\n • Professional development budget, conference sponsorship, and book reimbursement\n • Commuter benefits and monthly internet reimbursement\n\n •  Breakfast and lunch in our San Francisco office\n • A collaborative, in-person culture focused on learning, growth, and impact\n\n\n\nIf you find this role exciting, we encourage you to apply even if you think you don’t meet all of the requirements!\n\n\n\nWe are not accepting agency submissions or recruiting firm support for this role. Unsolicited resumes will not be considered.\n\n\n\nAirbyte is an equal opportunity employer that does not discriminate on the basis of actual or perceived race, creed, color, religion, national origin, ancestry, age, physical or mental disability, pregnancy, genetic information, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, marital status, familial status, domestic violence victim status, veteran or military status, or any other legally recognized protected basis under federal, state or local laws. Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.\n\n\n\nAirbyte is committed to providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities in our job application procedures. Please let us know if you need assistance or accommodations due to a disability."},{"id":"cbf66746-9e2a-4b23-a208-a6d78eb5ec63","title":"Senior Solutions Architect","department":"Sales","team":"Solutions Architecture ","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-15T21:39:06.598+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/airbyte/cbf66746-9e2a-4b23-a208-a6d78eb5ec63","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/airbyte/cbf66746-9e2a-4b23-a208-a6d78eb5ec63/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Airbyte is the data and action layer for AI agents. We give agents fast, accurate, authenticated access to business data across hundreds of sources, so they can discover the entities that matter, reason over real-time context, and take action in the systems they read from, not just observe them.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We started as the open-source standard for data movement and proved the economics of data integration at scale: hundreds of connectors, thousands of companies, and, since 2020, have raised $181M from leading investors including Benchmark, Accel, Altimeter, Coatue, and Y Combinator. As our CEO Michel Tricot puts it, \"the last ten years were all about structured data. The future is all about context.\" We're now building that context infrastructure for production-grade agents on the same open foundation, as agents become the primary consumers of enterprise data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our mission is unchanged: make data available and actionable to everyone, everywhere. That everyone now includes AI agents.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h2>The Role</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As an Airbyte Senior Solutions Architect, you will serve as a trusted post-sales technical partner to enterprise customers, helping them successfully onboard, implement, adopt, and expand their use of Airbyte.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will own the technical customer relationship after the sale, working closely with customer engineering, platform, infrastructure, and data teams to understand their environment, guide implementation, troubleshoot issues, and ensure they are getting long-term value from Airbyte.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is also a highly hands-on technical role. A major part of the job involves working directly in customer Kubernetes environments to deploy, configure, troubleshoot, and optimize Airbyte in production. You should be comfortable getting into the weeds with customers across workloads, pods, networking, storage, resource management, APIs, databases, CDC, and data movement issues.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will act as the bridge between customers and Airbyte’s Support, Product, Engineering, and Sales teams, serving as the internal source of truth for customer technical needs while helping drive adoption, retention, and expansion.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Joining Airbyte at this stage means working at the intersection of data infrastructure, cloud platforms, and AI while helping shape how enterprise customers successfully deploy and scale our products.</p><h2><br />What You’ll Do</h2><h3>Own Post-Sales Technical Success</h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the primary technical partner for enterprise customers after the sale, owning the technical relationship throughout onboarding, implementation, adoption, and expansion.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build trusted relationships with customer engineering, infrastructure, platform, and data teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop a deep understanding of each customer’s architecture, use cases, technical requirements, and long-term goals.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Guide customers through implementation and adoption while proactively identifying risks, blockers, and opportunities to improve their deployment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with customers to define technical success and ensure they are realizing measurable value from Airbyte.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate with Airbyte Support, Product, and Engineering to resolve complex customer issues and drive successful outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as the internal source of truth for customer technical requirements, infrastructure constraints, product feedback, and feature needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify opportunities for broader adoption and expansion in partnership with Sales and Customer Success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build long-term technical relationships that improve customer satisfaction, retention, and growth.</p></li></ul><h3>Hands-On Kubernetes &amp; Technical Implementation</h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work directly in customer Kubernetes environments to deploy, configure, troubleshoot, and optimize Airbyte in production.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Troubleshoot Kubernetes workloads, pods, deployments, networking, storage, resource allocation, scheduling, logs, and performance issues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Diagnose complex production issues across Kubernetes clusters and work alongside customer engineering teams to identify root causes and implement solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help customers apply Kubernetes best practices related to reliability, scalability, observability, and resource management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead technical implementation projects and ensure Airbyte is configured successfully within customer infrastructure, security, and operational requirements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Troubleshoot complex data movement issues involving SQL databases, CDC, database replication, and data synchronization.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with REST APIs, HTTP, authentication, OAuth, API keys, JWT, webhooks, and JSON to diagnose and resolve integration issues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advise customers on integrating LLM-based tooling and AI workflows into their existing data infrastructure alongside Airbyte connectors.</p></li></ul><h3>Cross-Functional Collaboration</h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with Product and Engineering to surface recurring customer challenges and influence the roadmap.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with Support to resolve complex technical issues and improve escalation paths.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with Sales to identify technical opportunities for expansion within existing customers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help improve onboarding playbooks, implementation guides, troubleshooting documentation, and customer best practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Share customer feedback and technical insights internally to improve the overall enterprise customer experience.</p></li></ul><h3>Advocacy and Evangelism</h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrate Airbyte architecture, implementation patterns, and best practices to customers and at industry events.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as a technical ambassador for Airbyte with customers and the broader developer and data community.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evangelize best practices for building reliable, scalable, and AI-ready data infrastructure.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create technical content such as blog posts, demos, implementation guides, and conference talks.</p></li></ul><h2>What You’ll Need</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6+ years of experience in a customer-facing post-sales technical role such as Solutions Architect, Technical Account Manager, Resident Solutions Architect, Professional Services Engineer, Customer Engineer, or technical consultant.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience owning long-term technical relationships with enterprise customers across onboarding, implementation, adoption, troubleshooting, and expansion.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong, hands-on Kubernetes experience in production environments. You should be comfortable independently troubleshooting workloads, pods, deployments, networking, storage, resource management, logs, and cluster-level issues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience deploying, operating, or troubleshooting applications running on Kubernetes, not just designing or advising on Kubernetes architecture.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of cloud infrastructure and production systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep understanding of database technologies, including SQL, CDC, database replication, and data synchronization.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong knowledge of REST APIs, HTTP, authentication, OAuth, API keys, JWT, webhooks, and JSON.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience in a startup environment, ideally within modern data infrastructure, cloud infrastructure, databases, ELT/ETL, developer tools, or data warehouses.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting technically complex products that directly impact customer operations or business productivity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong customer orientation with a track record of driving successful onboarding, implementation, adoption, and ongoing technical outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong interpersonal, communication, and presentation skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to build credibility with engineers while also communicating effectively with technical leadership and business stakeholders.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to Have</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Terraform, Helm, cloud networking, or infrastructure-as-code.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with AWS, GCP, or Azure.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with observability, monitoring, and debugging production infrastructure.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with one or more AI or LLM frameworks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to AI agent frameworks, MCP, or prompt engineering.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with modern data infrastructure, ELT tools, data warehouses, or distributed systems.</p></li></ul><h2>Location</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remote from New York City / East Coast timezone.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Why You'll Love Working at Airbyte:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Airbyte, we believe great work happens when people feel supported, trusted, and empowered to grow. Our market-leading Total Rewards package is designed to help you thrive professionally and personally. Our benefits and perks include:</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Flexible PTO with a culture that encourages at least 25 days off annually<br /> • 16 weeks fully paid parental leave for all parents<br /> • Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and dependents<br /> • 401(k) retirement plan<br /> • Professional development budget, conference sponsorship, and book reimbursement<br /> • Commuter benefits and monthly internet reimbursement</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> •  Breakfast and lunch in our San Francisco office<br /> • A collaborative, in-person culture focused on learning, growth, and impact</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you find this role exciting, we encourage you to apply even if you think you don’t meet all of the requirements!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are not accepting agency submissions or recruiting firm support for this role. Unsolicited resumes will not be considered.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Airbyte is an equal opportunity employer that does not discriminate on the basis of actual or perceived race, creed, color, religion, national origin, ancestry, age, physical or mental disability, pregnancy, genetic information, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, marital status, familial status, domestic violence victim status, veteran or military status, or any other legally recognized protected basis under federal, state or local laws. Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Airbyte is committed to providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities in our job application procedures. Please let us know if you need assistance or accommodations due to a disability.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Airbyte is the data and action layer for AI agents. We give agents fast, accurate, authenticated access to business data across hundreds of sources, so they can discover the entities that matter, reason over real-time context, and take action in the systems they read from, not just observe them.\n\n\n\nWe started as the open-source standard for data movement and proved the economics of data integration at scale: hundreds of connectors, thousands of companies, and, since 2020, have raised $181M from leading investors including Benchmark, Accel, Altimeter, Coatue, and Y Combinator. As our CEO Michel Tricot puts it, \"the last ten years were all about structured data. The future is all about context.\" We're now building that context infrastructure for production-grade agents on the same open foundation, as agents become the primary consumers of enterprise data.\n\n\n\nOur mission is unchanged: make data available and actionable to everyone, everywhere. That everyone now includes AI agents.\n\n \n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nAs an Airbyte Senior Solutions Architect, you will serve as a trusted post-sales technical partner to enterprise customers, helping them successfully onboard, implement, adopt, and expand their use of Airbyte.\n\nYou will own the technical customer relationship after the sale, working closely with customer engineering, platform, infrastructure, and data teams to understand their environment, guide implementation, troubleshoot issues, and ensure they are getting long-term value from Airbyte.\n\nThis is also a highly hands-on technical role. A major part of the job involves working directly in customer Kubernetes environments to deploy, configure, troubleshoot, and optimize Airbyte in production. You should be comfortable getting into the weeds with customers across workloads, pods, networking, storage, resource management, APIs, databases, CDC, and data movement issues.\n\nYou will act as the bridge between customers and Airbyte’s Support, Product, Engineering, and Sales teams, serving as the internal source of truth for customer technical needs while helping drive adoption, retention, and expansion.\n\nJoining Airbyte at this stage means working at the intersection of data infrastructure, cloud platforms, and AI while helping shape how enterprise customers successfully deploy and scale our products.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n\nOWN POST-SALES TECHNICAL SUCCESS\n\n - Serve as the primary technical partner for enterprise customers after the sale, owning the technical relationship throughout onboarding, implementation, adoption, and expansion.\n\n - Build trusted relationships with customer engineering, infrastructure, platform, and data teams.\n\n - Develop a deep understanding of each customer’s architecture, use cases, technical requirements, and long-term goals.\n\n - Guide customers through implementation and adoption while proactively identifying risks, blockers, and opportunities to improve their deployment.\n\n - Partner with customers to define technical success and ensure they are realizing measurable value from Airbyte.\n\n - Coordinate with Airbyte Support, Product, and Engineering to resolve complex customer issues and drive successful outcomes.\n\n - Act as the internal source of truth for customer technical requirements, infrastructure constraints, product feedback, and feature needs.\n\n - Identify opportunities for broader adoption and expansion in partnership with Sales and Customer Success.\n\n - Build long-term technical relationships that improve customer satisfaction, retention, and growth.\n\n\nHANDS-ON KUBERNETES & TECHNICAL IMPLEMENTATION\n\n - Work directly in customer Kubernetes environments to deploy, configure, troubleshoot, and optimize Airbyte in production.\n\n - Troubleshoot Kubernetes workloads, pods, deployments, networking, storage, resource allocation, scheduling, logs, and performance issues.\n\n - Diagnose complex production issues across Kubernetes clusters and work alongside customer engineering teams to identify root causes and implement solutions.\n\n - Help customers apply Kubernetes best practices related to reliability, scalability, observability, and resource management.\n\n - Lead technical implementation projects and ensure Airbyte is configured successfully within customer infrastructure, security, and operational requirements.\n\n - Troubleshoot complex data movement issues involving SQL databases, CDC, database replication, and data synchronization.\n\n - Work with REST APIs, HTTP, authentication, OAuth, API keys, JWT, webhooks, and JSON to diagnose and resolve integration issues.\n\n - Advise customers on integrating LLM-based tooling and AI workflows into their existing data infrastructure alongside Airbyte connectors.\n\n\nCROSS-FUNCTIONAL COLLABORATION\n\n - Partner closely with Product and Engineering to surface recurring customer challenges and influence the roadmap.\n\n - Collaborate with Support to resolve complex technical issues and improve escalation paths.\n\n - Work with Sales to identify technical opportunities for expansion within existing customers.\n\n - Help improve onboarding playbooks, implementation guides, troubleshooting documentation, and customer best practices.\n\n - Share customer feedback and technical insights internally to improve the overall enterprise customer experience.\n\n\nADVOCACY AND EVANGELISM\n\n - Demonstrate Airbyte architecture, implementation patterns, and best practices to customers and at industry events.\n\n - Serve as a technical ambassador for Airbyte with customers and the broader developer and data community.\n\n - Evangelize best practices for building reliable, scalable, and AI-ready data infrastructure.\n\n - Create technical content such as blog posts, demos, implementation guides, and conference talks.\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL NEED\n\n - 6+ years of experience in a customer-facing post-sales technical role such as Solutions Architect, Technical Account Manager, Resident Solutions Architect, Professional Services Engineer, Customer Engineer, or technical consultant.\n\n - Experience owning long-term technical relationships with enterprise customers across onboarding, implementation, adoption, troubleshooting, and expansion.\n\n - Strong, hands-on Kubernetes experience in production environments. You should be comfortable independently troubleshooting workloads, pods, deployments, networking, storage, resource management, logs, and cluster-level issues.\n\n - Experience deploying, operating, or troubleshooting applications running on Kubernetes, not just designing or advising on Kubernetes architecture.\n\n - Strong understanding of cloud infrastructure and production systems.\n\n - Deep understanding of database technologies, including SQL, CDC, database replication, and data synchronization.\n\n - Strong knowledge of REST APIs, HTTP, authentication, OAuth, API keys, JWT, webhooks, and JSON.\n\n - 2+ years of experience in a startup environment, ideally within modern data infrastructure, cloud infrastructure, databases, ELT/ETL, developer tools, or data warehouses.\n\n - Experience supporting technically complex products that directly impact customer operations or business productivity.\n\n - Strong customer orientation with a track record of driving successful onboarding, implementation, adoption, and ongoing technical outcomes.\n\n - Strong interpersonal, communication, and presentation skills.\n\n - Ability to build credibility with engineers while also communicating effectively with technical leadership and business stakeholders.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with Terraform, Helm, cloud networking, or infrastructure-as-code.\n\n - Experience with AWS, GCP, or Azure.\n\n - Experience with observability, monitoring, and debugging production infrastructure.\n\n - Hands-on experience with one or more AI or LLM frameworks.\n\n - Exposure to AI agent frameworks, MCP, or prompt engineering.\n\n - Experience with modern data infrastructure, ELT tools, data warehouses, or distributed systems.\n\n\nLOCATION\n\n - Remote from New York City / East Coast timezone.\n\n\n\n\nWHY YOU'LL LOVE WORKING AT AIRBYTE:\n\nAt Airbyte, we believe great work happens when people feel supported, trusted, and empowered to grow. Our market-leading Total Rewards package is designed to help you thrive professionally and personally. Our benefits and perks include:\n\n\n\n• Flexible PTO with a culture that encourages at least 25 days off annually\n • 16 weeks fully paid parental leave for all parents\n • Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and dependents\n • 401(k) retirement plan\n • Professional development budget, conference sponsorship, and book reimbursement\n • Commuter benefits and monthly internet reimbursement\n\n •  Breakfast and lunch in our San Francisco office\n • A collaborative, in-person culture focused on learning, growth, and impact\n\n\n\nIf you find this role exciting, we encourage you to apply even if you think you don’t meet all of the requirements!\n\n\n\nWe are not accepting agency submissions or recruiting firm support for this role. Unsolicited resumes will not be considered.\n\n\n\nAirbyte is an equal opportunity employer that does not discriminate on the basis of actual or perceived race, creed, color, religion, national origin, ancestry, age, physical or mental disability, pregnancy, genetic information, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, marital status, familial status, domestic violence victim status, veteran or military status, or any other legally recognized protected basis under federal, state or local laws. Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.\n\n\n\nAirbyte is committed to providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities in our job application procedures. Please let us know if you need assistance or accommodations due to a disability."},{"id":"44ea7c1a-a61b-4b41-bc41-009dd6349d83","title":"Senior Technical Account Manager","department":"Sales","team":"Sales","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York","secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-10T17:53:22.537+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/airbyte/44ea7c1a-a61b-4b41-bc41-009dd6349d83","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/airbyte/44ea7c1a-a61b-4b41-bc41-009dd6349d83/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Airbyte is the data and action layer for AI agents. We give agents fast, accurate, authenticated access to business data across hundreds of sources, so they can discover the entities that matter, reason over real-time context, and take action in the systems they read from, not just observe them.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We started as the open-source standard for data movement and proved the economics of data integration at scale: hundreds of connectors, thousands of companies, and, since 2020, have raised $181M from leading investors including Benchmark, Accel, Altimeter, Coatue, and Y Combinator. As our CEO Michel Tricot puts it, \"the last ten years were all about structured data. The future is all about context.\" We're now building that context infrastructure for production-grade agents on the same open foundation, as agents become the primary consumers of enterprise data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our mission is unchanged: make data available and actionable to everyone, everywhere. That everyone now includes AI agents.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h2><strong>The Role:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As an Airbyte Senior Technical Account Manager, you will have a unique opportunity to elevate your career and make an immediate impact in the rapidly growing data infrastructure sector. In this role, you will play a pivotal part in helping customers implement and adopt our products while serving as their advocate within the company. This includes collaborating with Go-to-Market (GTM), Product, and Engineering teams to refine and enhance the onboarding, implementation, and growth experiences for enterprise customers. You will also work closely with cross-functional teams to support both sales and post-sales efforts, driving improved qualification, faster deal cycles, and higher levels of customer satisfaction and retention. Joining us at this stage means you’ll be on the ground floor of a rapidly expanding Series B startup, with significant opportunities for professional growth and advancement.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h2><strong>What You’ll Do:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Technical Implementation</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead and execute impactful customer technical projects, including the implementation and deployment of Airbyte solutions, while ensuring alignment with client requirements and industry best practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Guide customers throughout their customer journey by leveraging your technical expertise and stepping in with hands-on support when needed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep Kubernetes expertise, including hands-on troubleshooting of workloads, pods, networking, storage, and resource management in production.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep understanding of database technologies, including SQL, CDC (Change Data Capture), database replication, and data synchronization concepts, with the ability to troubleshoot complex data movement issues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong knowledge of REST APIs, including HTTP methods, authentication (OAuth, API keys, JWT), webhooks, and JSON, with the ability to troubleshoot complex integration issues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advise customers on integrating LLM-based tooling into their existing data infrastructure alongside Airbyte connectors.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Client Engagement</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work directly with clients’ technical teams to understand their needs and tailor solutions accordingly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Managing technical success by collaborating with Airbyte’s technical support, Product, and Engineering teams to address issues and deliver new features.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help clients evaluate and adopt AI agent frameworks to build autonomous data agents that leverage Airbyte as a data source.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cross-Department Collaboration</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with Sales to identify and drive potential growth opportunities with customers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as the internal source of truth for customer technical requirements, expectations, and needed functionalities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Product and Engineering teams to surface customer needs, influencing the roadmap.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advocacy and Evangelism </p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrate the use and best practices of Airbyte’s offering to clients and at industry events.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as a brand ambassador promoting the organization’s mission and fostering relationships with key stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evangelize best practices for building AI-ready data stacks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create and deliver technical content (blog posts, demos, conference talks) showcasing how Airbyte enables modern AI architectures.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h2><strong>What You’ll Need:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6+ years of experience in a customer-facing technical role, such as Technical Account Manager, resident solutions architect, professional services engineer, or consulting role.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep, hands-on Kubernetes experience in production environments. You should be comfortable directly troubleshooting workloads, pods, networking, storage, resource allocation, and deployment issues rather than solely advising customers at a high level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience in a startup environment, ideally in modern data infrastructure, including cloud applications, databases, ELT tools, data warehouses or related fields (startup implementation experience is a bonus).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with one or more AI frameworks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to AI agent frameworks and prompt engineering best practices is a strong plus.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of supporting products that directly impact business productivity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional customer orientation with a focus on delivering seamless onboarding and ongoing technical success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong interpersonal and presentation skills.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h2><strong>Location:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remote from New York City, supporting East Coast Timezone</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Why You'll Love Working at Airbyte:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Airbyte, we believe great work happens when people feel supported, trusted, and empowered to grow. Our market-leading Total Rewards package is designed to help you thrive professionally and personally. Our benefits and perks include:</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Flexible PTO with a culture that encourages at least 25 days off annually<br /> • 16 weeks fully paid parental leave for all parents<br /> • Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and dependents<br /> • 401(k) retirement plan<br /> • Professional development budget, conference sponsorship, and book reimbursement<br /> • Commuter benefits and monthly internet reimbursement</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> •  Breakfast and lunch in our San Francisco office<br /> • A collaborative, in-person culture focused on learning, growth, and impact</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you find this role exciting, we encourage you to apply even if you think you don’t meet all of the requirements!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are not accepting agency submissions or recruiting firm support for this role. Unsolicited resumes will not be considered.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Airbyte is an equal opportunity employer that does not discriminate on the basis of actual or perceived race, creed, color, religion, national origin, ancestry, age, physical or mental disability, pregnancy, genetic information, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, marital status, familial status, domestic violence victim status, veteran or military status, or any other legally recognized protected basis under federal, state or local laws. Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Airbyte is committed to providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities in our job application procedures. Please let us know if you need assistance or accommodations due to a disability.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Airbyte is the data and action layer for AI agents. We give agents fast, accurate, authenticated access to business data across hundreds of sources, so they can discover the entities that matter, reason over real-time context, and take action in the systems they read from, not just observe them.\n\n\n\nWe started as the open-source standard for data movement and proved the economics of data integration at scale: hundreds of connectors, thousands of companies, and, since 2020, have raised $181M from leading investors including Benchmark, Accel, Altimeter, Coatue, and Y Combinator. As our CEO Michel Tricot puts it, \"the last ten years were all about structured data. The future is all about context.\" We're now building that context infrastructure for production-grade agents on the same open foundation, as agents become the primary consumers of enterprise data.\n\n\n\nOur mission is unchanged: make data available and actionable to everyone, everywhere. That everyone now includes AI agents.\n\n \n\n\nTHE ROLE:\n\nAs an Airbyte Senior Technical Account Manager, you will have a unique opportunity to elevate your career and make an immediate impact in the rapidly growing data infrastructure sector. In this role, you will play a pivotal part in helping customers implement and adopt our products while serving as their advocate within the company. This includes collaborating with Go-to-Market (GTM), Product, and Engineering teams to refine and enhance the onboarding, implementation, and growth experiences for enterprise customers. You will also work closely with cross-functional teams to support both sales and post-sales efforts, driving improved qualification, faster deal cycles, and higher levels of customer satisfaction and retention. Joining us at this stage means you’ll be on the ground floor of a rapidly expanding Series B startup, with significant opportunities for professional growth and advancement.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO:\n\nTechnical Implementation\n\n - Lead and execute impactful customer technical projects, including the implementation and deployment of Airbyte solutions, while ensuring alignment with client requirements and industry best practices.\n\n - Guide customers throughout their customer journey by leveraging your technical expertise and stepping in with hands-on support when needed.\n\n - Deep Kubernetes expertise, including hands-on troubleshooting of workloads, pods, networking, storage, and resource management in production.\n\n - Deep understanding of database technologies, including SQL, CDC (Change Data Capture), database replication, and data synchronization concepts, with the ability to troubleshoot complex data movement issues.\n\n - Strong knowledge of REST APIs, including HTTP methods, authentication (OAuth, API keys, JWT), webhooks, and JSON, with the ability to troubleshoot complex integration issues.\n\n - Advise customers on integrating LLM-based tooling into their existing data infrastructure alongside Airbyte connectors.\n\n\n\nClient Engagement\n\n - Work directly with clients’ technical teams to understand their needs and tailor solutions accordingly.\n\n - Managing technical success by collaborating with Airbyte’s technical support, Product, and Engineering teams to address issues and deliver new features.\n\n - Help clients evaluate and adopt AI agent frameworks to build autonomous data agents that leverage Airbyte as a data source.\n\n\n\nCross-Department Collaboration\n\n - Collaborate with Sales to identify and drive potential growth opportunities with customers.\n\n - Act as the internal source of truth for customer technical requirements, expectations, and needed functionalities.\n\n - Partner with Product and Engineering teams to surface customer needs, influencing the roadmap.\n\n\n\nAdvocacy and Evangelism \n\n - Demonstrate the use and best practices of Airbyte’s offering to clients and at industry events.\n\n - Serve as a brand ambassador promoting the organization’s mission and fostering relationships with key stakeholders.\n\n - Evangelize best practices for building AI-ready data stacks.\n\n - Create and deliver technical content (blog posts, demos, conference talks) showcasing how Airbyte enables modern AI architectures.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL NEED:\n\n - 6+ years of experience in a customer-facing technical role, such as Technical Account Manager, resident solutions architect, professional services engineer, or consulting role.\n\n - Deep, hands-on Kubernetes experience in production environments. You should be comfortable directly troubleshooting workloads, pods, networking, storage, resource allocation, and deployment issues rather than solely advising customers at a high level.\n\n - 2+ years of experience in a startup environment, ideally in modern data infrastructure, including cloud applications, databases, ELT tools, data warehouses or related fields (startup implementation experience is a bonus).\n\n - Hands-on experience with one or more AI frameworks.\n\n - Exposure to AI agent frameworks and prompt engineering best practices is a strong plus.\n\n - Proven track record of supporting products that directly impact business productivity.\n\n - Exceptional customer orientation with a focus on delivering seamless onboarding and ongoing technical success.\n\n - Strong interpersonal and presentation skills.\n\n \n \n\n\nLOCATION:\n\n - Remote from New York City, supporting East Coast Timezone\n\n\n\n\nWHY YOU'LL LOVE WORKING AT AIRBYTE:\n\nAt Airbyte, we believe great work happens when people feel supported, trusted, and empowered to grow. Our market-leading Total Rewards package is designed to help you thrive professionally and personally. Our benefits and perks include:\n\n\n\n• Flexible PTO with a culture that encourages at least 25 days off annually\n • 16 weeks fully paid parental leave for all parents\n • Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and dependents\n • 401(k) retirement plan\n • Professional development budget, conference sponsorship, and book reimbursement\n • Commuter benefits and monthly internet reimbursement\n\n •  Breakfast and lunch in our San Francisco office\n • A collaborative, in-person culture focused on learning, growth, and impact\n\n\n\nIf you find this role exciting, we encourage you to apply even if you think you don’t meet all of the requirements!\n\n\n\nWe are not accepting agency submissions or recruiting firm support for this role. Unsolicited resumes will not be considered.\n\n\n\nAirbyte is an equal opportunity employer that does not discriminate on the basis of actual or perceived race, creed, color, religion, national origin, ancestry, age, physical or mental disability, pregnancy, genetic information, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, marital status, familial status, domestic violence victim status, veteran or military status, or any other legally recognized protected basis under federal, state or local laws. Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.\n\n\n\nAirbyte is committed to providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities in our job application procedures. Please let us know if you need assistance or accommodations due to a disability."},{"id":"9b312680-5bcf-40b3-9cba-1023d2c9b895","title":"Senior Technical Account Manager","department":"Sales","team":"Sales","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Canada","secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-10T19:24:01.020+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Canada"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/airbyte/9b312680-5bcf-40b3-9cba-1023d2c9b895","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/airbyte/9b312680-5bcf-40b3-9cba-1023d2c9b895/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Airbyte is the data and action layer for AI agents. We give agents fast, accurate, authenticated access to business data across hundreds of sources, so they can discover the entities that matter, reason over real-time context, and take action in the systems they read from, not just observe them.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We started as the open-source standard for data movement and proved the economics of data integration at scale: hundreds of connectors, thousands of companies, and, since 2020, have raised $181M from leading investors including Benchmark, Accel, Altimeter, Coatue, and Y Combinator. As our CEO Michel Tricot puts it, \"the last ten years were all about structured data. The future is all about context.\" We're now building that context infrastructure for production-grade agents on the same open foundation, as agents become the primary consumers of enterprise data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our mission is unchanged: make data available and actionable to everyone, everywhere. That everyone now includes AI agents.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h2><strong>The Role:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As an Airbyte Senior Technical Account Manager, you will have a unique opportunity to elevate your career and make an immediate impact in the rapidly growing data infrastructure sector. In this role, you will play a pivotal part in helping customers implement and adopt our products while serving as their advocate within the company. This includes collaborating with Go-to-Market (GTM), Product, and Engineering teams to refine and enhance the onboarding, implementation, and growth experiences for enterprise customers. You will also work closely with cross-functional teams to support both sales and post-sales efforts, driving improved qualification, faster deal cycles, and higher levels of customer satisfaction and retention. Joining us at this stage means you’ll be on the ground floor of a rapidly expanding Series B startup, with significant opportunities for professional growth and advancement.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h2><strong>What You’ll Do:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Technical Implementation</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead and execute impactful customer technical projects, including the implementation and deployment of Airbyte solutions, while ensuring alignment with client requirements and industry best practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Guide customers throughout their customer journey by leveraging your technical expertise and stepping in with hands-on support when needed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep Kubernetes expertise, including hands-on troubleshooting of workloads, pods, networking, storage, and resource management in production.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep understanding of database technologies, including SQL, CDC (Change Data Capture), database replication, and data synchronization concepts, with the ability to troubleshoot complex data movement issues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong knowledge of REST APIs, including HTTP methods, authentication (OAuth, API keys, JWT), webhooks, and JSON, with the ability to troubleshoot complex integration issues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advise customers on integrating LLM-based tooling into their existing data infrastructure alongside Airbyte connectors.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Client Engagement</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work directly with clients’ technical teams to understand their needs and tailor solutions accordingly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Managing technical success by collaborating with Airbyte’s technical support, Product, and Engineering teams to address issues and deliver new features.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help clients evaluate and adopt AI agent frameworks to build autonomous data agents that leverage Airbyte as a data source.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cross-Department Collaboration</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with Sales to identify and drive potential growth opportunities with customers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Act as the internal source of truth for customer technical requirements, expectations, and needed functionalities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Product and Engineering teams to surface customer needs, influencing the roadmap.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advocacy and Evangelism </p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrate the use and best practices of Airbyte’s offering to clients and at industry events.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as a brand ambassador promoting the organization’s mission and fostering relationships with key stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evangelize best practices for building AI-ready data stacks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create and deliver technical content (blog posts, demos, conference talks) showcasing how Airbyte enables modern AI architectures.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h2><strong>What You’ll Need:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6+ years of experience in a customer-facing technical role, such as Technical Account Manager, resident solutions architect, professional services engineer, or consulting role.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep, hands-on Kubernetes experience in production environments. You should be comfortable directly troubleshooting workloads, pods, networking, storage, resource allocation, and deployment issues rather than solely advising customers at a high level.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of experience in a startup environment, ideally in modern data infrastructure, including cloud applications, databases, ELT tools, data warehouses or related fields (startup implementation experience is a bonus).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with one or more AI frameworks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to AI agent frameworks and prompt engineering best practices is a strong plus.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of supporting products that directly impact business productivity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional customer orientation with a focus on delivering seamless onboarding and ongoing technical success.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong interpersonal and presentation skills.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h2><strong>Location:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remote from Toronto, supporting East Coast Timezone</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Why You'll Love Working at Airbyte:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Airbyte, we believe great work happens when people feel supported, trusted, and empowered to grow. Our market-leading Total Rewards package is designed to help you thrive professionally and personally. Our benefits and perks include:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible PTO with a culture that encourages at least 25 days off annually, and public holidays in line with provincial employment standards</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comprehensive health coverage – extended health benefits on top of provincial public healthcare</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Virtual healthcare – access to doctors and other care providers online, so you can get care without waiting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Retirement savings – a group retirement savings plan to help you build for the future</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Statutory protections – Canada/Québec Pension Plan, Employment Insurance and workers' compensation coverage</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional development budget, conference sponsorship, and book reimbursement</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you find this role exciting, we encourage you to apply even if you think you don’t meet all of the requirements!</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are not accepting agency submissions or recruiting firm support for this role. Unsolicited resumes will not be considered.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Airbyte is the data and action layer for AI agents. We give agents fast, accurate, authenticated access to business data across hundreds of sources, so they can discover the entities that matter, reason over real-time context, and take action in the systems they read from, not just observe them.\n\n\n\nWe started as the open-source standard for data movement and proved the economics of data integration at scale: hundreds of connectors, thousands of companies, and, since 2020, have raised $181M from leading investors including Benchmark, Accel, Altimeter, Coatue, and Y Combinator. As our CEO Michel Tricot puts it, \"the last ten years were all about structured data. The future is all about context.\" We're now building that context infrastructure for production-grade agents on the same open foundation, as agents become the primary consumers of enterprise data.\n\n\n\nOur mission is unchanged: make data available and actionable to everyone, everywhere. That everyone now includes AI agents.\n\n \n\n\nTHE ROLE:\n\nAs an Airbyte Senior Technical Account Manager, you will have a unique opportunity to elevate your career and make an immediate impact in the rapidly growing data infrastructure sector. In this role, you will play a pivotal part in helping customers implement and adopt our products while serving as their advocate within the company. This includes collaborating with Go-to-Market (GTM), Product, and Engineering teams to refine and enhance the onboarding, implementation, and growth experiences for enterprise customers. You will also work closely with cross-functional teams to support both sales and post-sales efforts, driving improved qualification, faster deal cycles, and higher levels of customer satisfaction and retention. Joining us at this stage means you’ll be on the ground floor of a rapidly expanding Series B startup, with significant opportunities for professional growth and advancement.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO:\n\nTechnical Implementation\n\n - Lead and execute impactful customer technical projects, including the implementation and deployment of Airbyte solutions, while ensuring alignment with client requirements and industry best practices.\n\n - Guide customers throughout their customer journey by leveraging your technical expertise and stepping in with hands-on support when needed.\n\n - Deep Kubernetes expertise, including hands-on troubleshooting of workloads, pods, networking, storage, and resource management in production.\n\n - Deep understanding of database technologies, including SQL, CDC (Change Data Capture), database replication, and data synchronization concepts, with the ability to troubleshoot complex data movement issues.\n\n - Strong knowledge of REST APIs, including HTTP methods, authentication (OAuth, API keys, JWT), webhooks, and JSON, with the ability to troubleshoot complex integration issues.\n\n - Advise customers on integrating LLM-based tooling into their existing data infrastructure alongside Airbyte connectors.\n\n\n\nClient Engagement\n\n - Work directly with clients’ technical teams to understand their needs and tailor solutions accordingly.\n\n - Managing technical success by collaborating with Airbyte’s technical support, Product, and Engineering teams to address issues and deliver new features.\n\n - Help clients evaluate and adopt AI agent frameworks to build autonomous data agents that leverage Airbyte as a data source.\n\n\n\nCross-Department Collaboration\n\n - Collaborate with Sales to identify and drive potential growth opportunities with customers.\n\n - Act as the internal source of truth for customer technical requirements, expectations, and needed functionalities.\n\n - Partner with Product and Engineering teams to surface customer needs, influencing the roadmap.\n\n\n\nAdvocacy and Evangelism \n\n - Demonstrate the use and best practices of Airbyte’s offering to clients and at industry events.\n\n - Serve as a brand ambassador promoting the organization’s mission and fostering relationships with key stakeholders.\n\n - Evangelize best practices for building AI-ready data stacks.\n\n - Create and deliver technical content (blog posts, demos, conference talks) showcasing how Airbyte enables modern AI architectures.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL NEED:\n\n - 6+ years of experience in a customer-facing technical role, such as Technical Account Manager, resident solutions architect, professional services engineer, or consulting role.\n\n - Deep, hands-on Kubernetes experience in production environments. You should be comfortable directly troubleshooting workloads, pods, networking, storage, resource allocation, and deployment issues rather than solely advising customers at a high level.\n\n - 2+ years of experience in a startup environment, ideally in modern data infrastructure, including cloud applications, databases, ELT tools, data warehouses or related fields (startup implementation experience is a bonus).\n\n - Hands-on experience with one or more AI frameworks.\n\n - Exposure to AI agent frameworks and prompt engineering best practices is a strong plus.\n\n - Proven track record of supporting products that directly impact business productivity.\n\n - Exceptional customer orientation with a focus on delivering seamless onboarding and ongoing technical success.\n\n - Strong interpersonal and presentation skills.\n\n \n \n\n\nLOCATION:\n\n - Remote from Toronto, supporting East Coast Timezone\n\n\n\n\nWHY YOU'LL LOVE WORKING AT AIRBYTE:\n\nAt Airbyte, we believe great work happens when people feel supported, trusted, and empowered to grow. Our market-leading Total Rewards package is designed to help you thrive professionally and personally. Our benefits and perks include:\n\n - Flexible PTO with a culture that encourages at least 25 days off annually, and public holidays in line with provincial employment standards\n\n - Comprehensive health coverage – extended health benefits on top of provincial public healthcare\n\n - Virtual healthcare – access to doctors and other care providers online, so you can get care without waiting\n\n - Retirement savings – a group retirement savings plan to help you build for the future\n\n - Statutory protections – Canada/Québec Pension Plan, Employment Insurance and workers' compensation coverage\n\n - Professional development budget, conference sponsorship, and book reimbursement\n\n \n\nIf you find this role exciting, we encourage you to apply even if you think you don’t meet all of the requirements!\n\n \n\nWe are not accepting agency submissions or recruiting firm support for this role. Unsolicited resumes will not be considered."},{"id":"c595e670-8afb-47b3-9ba4-0efd11861e8c","title":"Technical Support Engineer","department":"Technical Support ","team":"Technical Support ","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Canada","secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-10-15T21:54:35.309+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Canada"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/airbyte/c595e670-8afb-47b3-9ba4-0efd11861e8c","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/airbyte/c595e670-8afb-47b3-9ba4-0efd11861e8c/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Airbyte is the data and action layer for AI agents. We give agents fast, accurate, authenticated access to business data across hundreds of sources, so they can discover the entities that matter, reason over real-time context, and take action in the systems they read from, not just observe them.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We started as the open-source standard for data movement and proved the economics of data integration at scale: hundreds of connectors, thousands of companies, and, since 2020, have raised $181M from leading investors including Benchmark, Accel, Altimeter, Coatue, and Y Combinator. As our CEO Michel Tricot puts it, \"the last ten years were all about structured data. The future is all about context.\" We're now building that context infrastructure for production-grade agents on the same open foundation, as agents become the primary consumers of enterprise data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our mission is unchanged: make data available and actionable to everyone, everywhere. That everyone now includes AI agents.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>The Role:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Do you get excited when a gnarly API issue finally clicks into place? Do you love being the person customers can count on when things get complicated? As a Technical Support Engineer at Airbyte, you'll bring together deep technical expertise and genuine customer empathy to support our growing cloud and embedded integration platform. You won't just be closing tickets, you'll be influencing how our product evolves by championing the customer voice with our engineering and product teams every day.</p><h2><br /><strong>What You’ll Do:</strong><br /></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Customer Support &amp; Troubleshooting</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be the person customers can count on, responding via email, ticketing systems, and the occasional video call with the kind of clarity and care that turns frustrated users into loyal ones.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Triage and prioritize incoming issues with urgency, consistently meeting SLA targets while leveraging AI tools to work smarter and resolve issues faster.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Dig into complex issues across APIs, connectors, data pipelines, and SaaS integrations, not just finding workarounds but partnering with Engineering to get to the root cause and drive real fixes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Document and reproduce customer-reported bugs with enough detail that the right people can act on them quickly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support embedded platform customers through onboarding and troubleshooting, including OAuth flows, widget tokens, scoped API tokens, and connector configuration.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">API &amp; Technical Expertise</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Get hands-on with customers who are building and debugging integrations, helping them navigate the Airbyte API and third-party APIs with confidence, from authentication and pagination to rate limiting, error handling, and webhooks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Test and validate API endpoints, review request/response payloads, and guide customers through integration best practices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support customers with the Embedded API and Airbyte MCP, covering source creation, connector template management, and widget token authentication.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help customers building on the Airbyte Connector SDK find their footing, including YAML-based connector definitions, OpenAPI specs, and cassette-based testing workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay sharp on Airbyte's API surface, new connector releases, and platform updates so your guidance is always accurate and timely.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cross-Functional Collaboration</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be the voice of the customer inside Airbyte, working closely with Engineering and Product to surface issues, advocate for feature requests, and make sure customer pain points actually influence the roadmap.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with the Engineering teams to relay platform-specific feedback, connector gaps, and SDK usability issues before they become bigger problems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Sales and Customer Success for technical conversations, onboarding, and expansion efforts, bringing the kind of product depth that helps close and retain customers.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge &amp; Process Improvement</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create and maintain internal and external knowledge base articles, troubleshooting guides, and API documentation to support scalability.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Document research and troubleshooting processes to aid in faster ticket resolution and team knowledge-sharing.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify opportunities for automation and process improvements with AI that reduce support load and improve the customer experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Spearhead initiatives to fill organizational or support gaps and take ownership of unique projects.<br /></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What You'll Need:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years in technical support, data engineering, DevOps, QA, or a similar role supporting developers or technical users.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with RESTful APIs and GraphQL, including OAuth, pagination, webhooks, rate limiting, and error handling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency with API testing tools like Postman or cURL.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of cloud platforms (AWS, GCP, or Azure) and data integration concepts including ELT/ETL workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong troubleshooting instincts, clear communication with both technical and non-technical stakeholders, and a growth mindset that keeps you improving even when things get hard.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated use of AI tools to speed up troubleshooting or automate a workflow, such as agents, MCP, or prompt and context engineering. Tell us what you built.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">High tolerance for ambiguity and a natural self-starter.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Nice To Have:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with Python, Java, or Kotlin and experience with CI/CD pipelines and GitHub.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with container orchestration tools like Kubernetes or Docker and multi-tenant architectures.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background supporting developer-facing or embedded/platform products in a B2B SaaS context.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with OpenAPI specs, YAML configuration, and Jinja expressions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with SQL and working knowledge of databases, including CDC setups.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Location:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remote in Canada (Eastern timezone)</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Why You'll Love Working at Airbyte:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Airbyte, we believe great work happens when people feel supported, trusted, and empowered to grow. Our market-leading Total Rewards package is designed to help you thrive professionally and personally. Our benefits and perks include:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible PTO with a culture that encourages at least 25 days off annually, and public holidays in line with provincial employment standards</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comprehensive health coverage – extended health benefits on top of provincial public healthcare</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Virtual healthcare – access to doctors and other care providers online, so you can get care without waiting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Retirement savings – a group retirement savings plan to help you build for the future</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Statutory protections – Canada/Québec Pension Plan, Employment Insurance and workers' compensation coverage</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional development budget, conference sponsorship, and book reimbursement</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you find this role exciting, we encourage you to apply even if you think you don’t meet all of the requirements!</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are not accepting agency submissions or recruiting firm support for this role. Unsolicited resumes will not be considered.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Airbyte is the data and action layer for AI agents. We give agents fast, accurate, authenticated access to business data across hundreds of sources, so they can discover the entities that matter, reason over real-time context, and take action in the systems they read from, not just observe them.\n\n\n\nWe started as the open-source standard for data movement and proved the economics of data integration at scale: hundreds of connectors, thousands of companies, and, since 2020, have raised $181M from leading investors including Benchmark, Accel, Altimeter, Coatue, and Y Combinator. As our CEO Michel Tricot puts it, \"the last ten years were all about structured data. The future is all about context.\" We're now building that context infrastructure for production-grade agents on the same open foundation, as agents become the primary consumers of enterprise data.\n\n\n\nOur mission is unchanged: make data available and actionable to everyone, everywhere. That everyone now includes AI agents.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE:\n\nDo you get excited when a gnarly API issue finally clicks into place? Do you love being the person customers can count on when things get complicated? As a Technical Support Engineer at Airbyte, you'll bring together deep technical expertise and genuine customer empathy to support our growing cloud and embedded integration platform. You won't just be closing tickets, you'll be influencing how our product evolves by championing the customer voice with our engineering and product teams every day.\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO:\n\n\nCustomer Support & Troubleshooting\n\n - Be the person customers can count on, responding via email, ticketing systems, and the occasional video call with the kind of clarity and care that turns frustrated users into loyal ones.\n\n - Triage and prioritize incoming issues with urgency, consistently meeting SLA targets while leveraging AI tools to work smarter and resolve issues faster.\n\n - Dig into complex issues across APIs, connectors, data pipelines, and SaaS integrations, not just finding workarounds but partnering with Engineering to get to the root cause and drive real fixes.\n\n - Document and reproduce customer-reported bugs with enough detail that the right people can act on them quickly.\n\n - Support embedded platform customers through onboarding and troubleshooting, including OAuth flows, widget tokens, scoped API tokens, and connector configuration.\n\n\n\nAPI & Technical Expertise\n\n - Get hands-on with customers who are building and debugging integrations, helping them navigate the Airbyte API and third-party APIs with confidence, from authentication and pagination to rate limiting, error handling, and webhooks.\n\n - Test and validate API endpoints, review request/response payloads, and guide customers through integration best practices.\n\n - Support customers with the Embedded API and Airbyte MCP, covering source creation, connector template management, and widget token authentication.\n\n - Help customers building on the Airbyte Connector SDK find their footing, including YAML-based connector definitions, OpenAPI specs, and cassette-based testing workflows.\n\n - Stay sharp on Airbyte's API surface, new connector releases, and platform updates so your guidance is always accurate and timely.\n\n\n\nCross-Functional Collaboration\n\n - Be the voice of the customer inside Airbyte, working closely with Engineering and Product to surface issues, advocate for feature requests, and make sure customer pain points actually influence the roadmap.\n\n - Partner with the Engineering teams to relay platform-specific feedback, connector gaps, and SDK usability issues before they become bigger problems.\n\n - Partner with Sales and Customer Success for technical conversations, onboarding, and expansion efforts, bringing the kind of product depth that helps close and retain customers.\n\n\n\nKnowledge & Process Improvement\n\n - Create and maintain internal and external knowledge base articles, troubleshooting guides, and API documentation to support scalability.\n\n - Document research and troubleshooting processes to aid in faster ticket resolution and team knowledge-sharing.\n\n - Identify opportunities for automation and process improvements with AI that reduce support load and improve the customer experience.\n\n - Spearhead initiatives to fill organizational or support gaps and take ownership of unique projects.\n   \n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL NEED:\n\n - 3+ years in technical support, data engineering, DevOps, QA, or a similar role supporting developers or technical users.\n\n - Hands-on experience with RESTful APIs and GraphQL, including OAuth, pagination, webhooks, rate limiting, and error handling.\n\n - Proficiency with API testing tools like Postman or cURL.\n\n - Understanding of cloud platforms (AWS, GCP, or Azure) and data integration concepts including ELT/ETL workflows.\n\n - Strong troubleshooting instincts, clear communication with both technical and non-technical stakeholders, and a growth mindset that keeps you improving even when things get hard.\n\n - Demonstrated use of AI tools to speed up troubleshooting or automate a workflow, such as agents, MCP, or prompt and context engineering. Tell us what you built.\n\n - High tolerance for ambiguity and a natural self-starter.\n\n\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE:\n\n - Familiarity with Python, Java, or Kotlin and experience with CI/CD pipelines and GitHub.\n\n - Experience with container orchestration tools like Kubernetes or Docker and multi-tenant architectures.\n\n - Background supporting developer-facing or embedded/platform products in a B2B SaaS context.\n\n - Familiarity with OpenAPI specs, YAML configuration, and Jinja expressions.\n\n - Experience with SQL and working knowledge of databases, including CDC setups.\n\n\n\n\nLOCATION:\n\n - Remote in Canada (Eastern timezone)\n\n\n\n\nWHY YOU'LL LOVE WORKING AT AIRBYTE:\n\nAt Airbyte, we believe great work happens when people feel supported, trusted, and empowered to grow. Our market-leading Total Rewards package is designed to help you thrive professionally and personally. Our benefits and perks include:\n\n - Flexible PTO with a culture that encourages at least 25 days off annually, and public holidays in line with provincial employment standards\n\n - Comprehensive health coverage – extended health benefits on top of provincial public healthcare\n\n - Virtual healthcare – access to doctors and other care providers online, so you can get care without waiting\n\n - Retirement savings – a group retirement savings plan to help you build for the future\n\n - Statutory protections – Canada/Québec Pension Plan, Employment Insurance and workers' compensation coverage\n\n - Professional development budget, conference sponsorship, and book reimbursement\n\n \n\nIf you find this role exciting, we encourage you to apply even if you think you don’t meet all of the requirements!\n\n \n\nWe are not accepting agency submissions or recruiting firm support for this role. Unsolicited resumes will not be considered."},{"id":"9d81a132-966b-4f37-b198-d950e23a7765","title":"Customer Support Developer (Databases)","department":"Technical Support ","team":"Technical Support ","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-10-08T18:32:02.204+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/airbyte/9d81a132-966b-4f37-b198-d950e23a7765","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/airbyte/9d81a132-966b-4f37-b198-d950e23a7765/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Airbyte is the data and action layer for AI agents. We give agents fast, accurate, authenticated access to business data across hundreds of sources, so they can discover the entities that matter, reason over real-time context, and take action in the systems they read from, not just observe them.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We started as the open-source standard for data movement and proved the economics of data integration at scale: hundreds of connectors, thousands of companies, and, since 2020, have raised $181M from leading investors including Benchmark, Accel, Altimeter, Coatue, and Y Combinator. As our CEO Michel Tricot puts it, \"the last ten years were all about structured data. The future is all about context.\" We're now building that context infrastructure for production-grade agents on the same open foundation, as agents become the primary consumers of enterprise data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our mission is unchanged: make data available and actionable to everyone, everywhere. That everyone now includes AI agents.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>The Role:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Are you the kind of developer who gets a rush from cracking a gnarly replication bug, an issue with CDC implementation, or a query that hangs with no obvious reason? Do you thrive at the intersection of writing code and helping customers succeed? As a Customer Support Developer (Databases) at Airbyte, you'll combine hands-on development skills with deep technical empathy to support our growing cloud, embedded, and open-source integration platform. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This isn't a traditional support role. You'll be writing Java and Kotlin, shipping contributions to our open-source database source and destination connectors, digging into query plans and transaction logs, and directly shaping how customers move mission-critical data between databases, warehouses, and lakes. You'll champion the customer voice alongside our engineering and product teams every day, getting your hands dirty in the code.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What You’ll Do:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Customer Support &amp; Technical Troubleshooting</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the primary technical escalation point for database-related customer issues, responding via email, ticketing systems, and video calls with precision and clarity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Triage and prioritize incoming issues with urgency, consistently meeting SLA targets while leveraging AI tools to work smarter and resolve issues faster.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Dig into complex issues across relational databases, data warehouses, data lakes, and cloud object storage, not just finding workarounds but partnering with Engineering to root-cause and drive real fixes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reproduce customer-reported bugs by inspecting connector logs, query plans, replication slots, transaction logs, sync state, and destination table state, and document findings with enough technical detail for Engineering to act on immediately.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support customers through onboarding and troubleshooting for SSH tunnels, network configuration, database user permissions, CDC setup (WAL/binlog/redo logs), and warehouse/lake authentication.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Database Connector Development</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Get hands-on with customers building and debugging integrations, helping them navigate Airbyte's database sources and destinations with confidence, from authentication and SSL/SSH setup to CDC, schema evolution, incremental cursors, and typed destination tables.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Validate database version compatibility across supported engines and releases, maintain testing environments, and reproduce customer-reported behavior on real database and warehouse instances.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support customers writing to data warehouses (Snowflake, BigQuery, Redshift), data lakes and object storage (S3, GCS, Azure Blob, Databricks, Iceberg), and databases (Postgres, MySQL, MSSQL, ClickHouse), including schema evolution and typed-columns behavior.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help customers running database sources (PostgreSQL, MySQL, MSSQL, Oracle, MongoDB, and more) troubleshoot replication behavior, cursor selection, full-refresh vs. incremental vs. CDC trade-offs, and sync state recovery.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute directly to Airbyte's open-source database connectors and the Java/Kotlin Bulk CDK: fix bugs, improve error handling, harden schema-evolution and CDC paths, and submit pull requests to the Airbyte repository.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review and test community contributions to database sources and destinations, helping external contributors land high-quality changes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay sharp on Airbyte's connector catalog, new database and destination releases, and platform updates so your guidance is always accurate and timely.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cross-Functional Collaboration &amp; Enablement</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be the voice of the customer within Airbyte, working closely with Engineering and Product to surface issues, advocate for feature requests, and ensure customer pain points actually influence the database reliability and performance roadmap.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Solutions Engineering and Sales Engineering to provide white-glove technical onboarding for enterprise customers, including CDC architecture reviews, destination schema modeling, and production readiness assessments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Train and mentor Technical Support Engineers on database connector concepts, including JDBC fundamentals, CDC patterns, schema evolution, query optimization, destination typing and normalization, and the Airbyte protocol (spec, discover, check, read, write).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Sales and Customer Success for technical conversations, onboarding, and expansion efforts, bringing the kind of product depth that helps close and retain customers.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge, Process Improvement, &amp; AI </p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create and maintain internal and external knowledge base articles, troubleshooting guides, and database connector documentation to support scalability.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Document research and troubleshooting processes,( including CDC debugging, destination schema reconciliation, and performance tuning runbooks), to aid faster ticket resolution and team knowledge sharing.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify AI-driven opportunities for automation and process improvements that reduce support load and improve the customer experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Embrace AI-assisted workflows and contribute to developing playbooks and skills that encode repeatable troubleshooting procedures, connector debugging patterns, and onboarding Runbooks, enabling the team to scale expertise through automation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Spearhead initiatives to fill organizational or support gaps and take ownership of unique projects.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What You’ll Need:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years in software engineering, data engineering, technical support, DevOps, QA, or a similar role supporting developers or technical users.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency in SQL, with hands-on experience investigating query plans, isolation levels, and performance bottlenecks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency in Java or Kotlin. You must be able to read, write, and debug JVM-based connector code. You'll be contributing to database sources and destinations, the Bulk CDK, and automation tooling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with relational databases, data warehouses, or data lakes, including concepts like CDC (Change Data Capture), schema evolution, and query optimization.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with JDBC and common database drivers, and comfort debugging connection, authentication, SSL, and SSH tunnel issues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of cloud platforms (AWS, GCP, or Azure) and data integration concepts, including ELT/ETL workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong troubleshooting instincts, clear communication with both technical and non-technical stakeholders, and a growth mindset that keeps you improving even when things get hard.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">High tolerance for ambiguity and a natural self-starter.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Nice To Have:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with PostgreSQL, MySQL, MSSQL, Oracle, MongoDB, Snowflake, BigQuery, Redshift, ClickHouse, or similar relational and non-relational systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with data lakes and open table formats (Iceberg, Delta Lake), and cloud object storage (S3, GCS, Azure Blob).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with Airbyte's Bulk CDK or contributions to open-source database connectors.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with container orchestration tools like Kubernetes or Docker and multi-tenant architectures.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background supporting developer-facing or embedded/platform products in a B2B SaaS context.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with CI/CD pipelines and GitHub-based open-source workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with AI-assisted development tools and building automated playbooks or Runbooks.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Location:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remote in U.S.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Why You'll Love Working at Airbyte:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Airbyte, we believe great work happens when people feel supported, trusted, and empowered to grow. Our market-leading Total Rewards package is designed to help you thrive professionally and personally. Our benefits and perks include:</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">• Flexible PTO with a culture that encourages at least 25 days off annually<br /> • 16 weeks fully paid parental leave for all parents<br /> • Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and dependents<br /> • 401(k) retirement plan<br /> • Professional development budget, conference sponsorship, and book reimbursement<br /> • Commuter benefits and monthly internet reimbursement</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> •  Breakfast and lunch in our San Francisco office<br /> • A collaborative, in-person culture focused on learning, growth, and impact</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you find this role exciting, we encourage you to apply even if you think you don’t meet all of the requirements!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are not accepting agency submissions or recruiting firm support for this role. Unsolicited resumes will not be considered.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Airbyte is an equal opportunity employer that does not discriminate on the basis of actual or perceived race, creed, color, religion, national origin, ancestry, age, physical or mental disability, pregnancy, genetic information, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, marital status, familial status, domestic violence victim status, veteran or military status, or any other legally recognized protected basis under federal, state or local laws. Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Airbyte is committed to providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities in our job application procedures. Please let us know if you need assistance or accommodations due to a disability.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Airbyte is the data and action layer for AI agents. We give agents fast, accurate, authenticated access to business data across hundreds of sources, so they can discover the entities that matter, reason over real-time context, and take action in the systems they read from, not just observe them.\n\n\n\nWe started as the open-source standard for data movement and proved the economics of data integration at scale: hundreds of connectors, thousands of companies, and, since 2020, have raised $181M from leading investors including Benchmark, Accel, Altimeter, Coatue, and Y Combinator. As our CEO Michel Tricot puts it, \"the last ten years were all about structured data. The future is all about context.\" We're now building that context infrastructure for production-grade agents on the same open foundation, as agents become the primary consumers of enterprise data.\n\n\n\nOur mission is unchanged: make data available and actionable to everyone, everywhere. That everyone now includes AI agents.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE:\n\nAre you the kind of developer who gets a rush from cracking a gnarly replication bug, an issue with CDC implementation, or a query that hangs with no obvious reason? Do you thrive at the intersection of writing code and helping customers succeed? As a Customer Support Developer (Databases) at Airbyte, you'll combine hands-on development skills with deep technical empathy to support our growing cloud, embedded, and open-source integration platform. \n\n\n\nThis isn't a traditional support role. You'll be writing Java and Kotlin, shipping contributions to our open-source database source and destination connectors, digging into query plans and transaction logs, and directly shaping how customers move mission-critical data between databases, warehouses, and lakes. You'll champion the customer voice alongside our engineering and product teams every day, getting your hands dirty in the code.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO:\n\nCustomer Support & Technical Troubleshooting\n\n - Serve as the primary technical escalation point for database-related customer issues, responding via email, ticketing systems, and video calls with precision and clarity.\n\n - Triage and prioritize incoming issues with urgency, consistently meeting SLA targets while leveraging AI tools to work smarter and resolve issues faster.\n\n - Dig into complex issues across relational databases, data warehouses, data lakes, and cloud object storage, not just finding workarounds but partnering with Engineering to root-cause and drive real fixes.\n\n - Reproduce customer-reported bugs by inspecting connector logs, query plans, replication slots, transaction logs, sync state, and destination table state, and document findings with enough technical detail for Engineering to act on immediately.\n\n - Support customers through onboarding and troubleshooting for SSH tunnels, network configuration, database user permissions, CDC setup (WAL/binlog/redo logs), and warehouse/lake authentication.\n\n\n\nDatabase Connector Development\n\n - Get hands-on with customers building and debugging integrations, helping them navigate Airbyte's database sources and destinations with confidence, from authentication and SSL/SSH setup to CDC, schema evolution, incremental cursors, and typed destination tables.\n\n - Validate database version compatibility across supported engines and releases, maintain testing environments, and reproduce customer-reported behavior on real database and warehouse instances.\n\n - Support customers writing to data warehouses (Snowflake, BigQuery, Redshift), data lakes and object storage (S3, GCS, Azure Blob, Databricks, Iceberg), and databases (Postgres, MySQL, MSSQL, ClickHouse), including schema evolution and typed-columns behavior.\n\n - Help customers running database sources (PostgreSQL, MySQL, MSSQL, Oracle, MongoDB, and more) troubleshoot replication behavior, cursor selection, full-refresh vs. incremental vs. CDC trade-offs, and sync state recovery.\n\n - Contribute directly to Airbyte's open-source database connectors and the Java/Kotlin Bulk CDK: fix bugs, improve error handling, harden schema-evolution and CDC paths, and submit pull requests to the Airbyte repository.\n\n - Review and test community contributions to database sources and destinations, helping external contributors land high-quality changes.\n\n - Stay sharp on Airbyte's connector catalog, new database and destination releases, and platform updates so your guidance is always accurate and timely.\n\n\n\nCross-Functional Collaboration & Enablement\n\n - Be the voice of the customer within Airbyte, working closely with Engineering and Product to surface issues, advocate for feature requests, and ensure customer pain points actually influence the database reliability and performance roadmap.\n\n - Partner with Solutions Engineering and Sales Engineering to provide white-glove technical onboarding for enterprise customers, including CDC architecture reviews, destination schema modeling, and production readiness assessments.\n\n - Train and mentor Technical Support Engineers on database connector concepts, including JDBC fundamentals, CDC patterns, schema evolution, query optimization, destination typing and normalization, and the Airbyte protocol (spec, discover, check, read, write).\n\n - Partner with Sales and Customer Success for technical conversations, onboarding, and expansion efforts, bringing the kind of product depth that helps close and retain customers.\n\n\n\nKnowledge, Process Improvement, & AI \n\n - Create and maintain internal and external knowledge base articles, troubleshooting guides, and database connector documentation to support scalability.\n\n - Document research and troubleshooting processes,( including CDC debugging, destination schema reconciliation, and performance tuning runbooks), to aid faster ticket resolution and team knowledge sharing.\n\n - Identify AI-driven opportunities for automation and process improvements that reduce support load and improve the customer experience.\n\n - Embrace AI-assisted workflows and contribute to developing playbooks and skills that encode repeatable troubleshooting procedures, connector debugging patterns, and onboarding Runbooks, enabling the team to scale expertise through automation.\n\n - Spearhead initiatives to fill organizational or support gaps and take ownership of unique projects.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL NEED:\n\n - 2+ years in software engineering, data engineering, technical support, DevOps, QA, or a similar role supporting developers or technical users.\n\n - Fluency in SQL, with hands-on experience investigating query plans, isolation levels, and performance bottlenecks.\n\n - Proficiency in Java or Kotlin. You must be able to read, write, and debug JVM-based connector code. You'll be contributing to database sources and destinations, the Bulk CDK, and automation tooling.\n\n - Hands-on experience with relational databases, data warehouses, or data lakes, including concepts like CDC (Change Data Capture), schema evolution, and query optimization.\n\n - Experience with JDBC and common database drivers, and comfort debugging connection, authentication, SSL, and SSH tunnel issues.\n\n - Understanding of cloud platforms (AWS, GCP, or Azure) and data integration concepts, including ELT/ETL workflows.\n\n - Strong troubleshooting instincts, clear communication with both technical and non-technical stakeholders, and a growth mindset that keeps you improving even when things get hard.\n\n - High tolerance for ambiguity and a natural self-starter.\n\n\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE:\n\n - Experience with PostgreSQL, MySQL, MSSQL, Oracle, MongoDB, Snowflake, BigQuery, Redshift, ClickHouse, or similar relational and non-relational systems.\n\n - Experience with data lakes and open table formats (Iceberg, Delta Lake), and cloud object storage (S3, GCS, Azure Blob).\n\n - Familiarity with Airbyte's Bulk CDK or contributions to open-source database connectors.\n\n - Experience with container orchestration tools like Kubernetes or Docker and multi-tenant architectures.\n\n - Background supporting developer-facing or embedded/platform products in a B2B SaaS context.\n\n - Experience with CI/CD pipelines and GitHub-based open-source workflows.\n\n - Experience with AI-assisted development tools and building automated playbooks or Runbooks.\n\n\n\n\nLOCATION:\n\n - Remote in U.S.\n\n\n\n\nWHY YOU'LL LOVE WORKING AT AIRBYTE:\n\nAt Airbyte, we believe great work happens when people feel supported, trusted, and empowered to grow. Our market-leading Total Rewards package is designed to help you thrive professionally and personally. Our benefits and perks include:\n\n\n\n• Flexible PTO with a culture that encourages at least 25 days off annually\n • 16 weeks fully paid parental leave for all parents\n • Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and dependents\n • 401(k) retirement plan\n • Professional development budget, conference sponsorship, and book reimbursement\n • Commuter benefits and monthly internet reimbursement\n\n •  Breakfast and lunch in our San Francisco office\n • A collaborative, in-person culture focused on learning, growth, and impact\n\n\n\nIf you find this role exciting, we encourage you to apply even if you think you don’t meet all of the requirements!\n\n\n\nWe are not accepting agency submissions or recruiting firm support for this role. Unsolicited resumes will not be considered.\n\n\n\nAirbyte is an equal opportunity employer that does not discriminate on the basis of actual or perceived race, creed, color, religion, national origin, ancestry, age, physical or mental disability, pregnancy, genetic information, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, marital status, familial status, domestic violence victim status, veteran or military status, or any other legally recognized protected basis under federal, state or local laws. Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.\n\n\n\nAirbyte is committed to providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities in our job application procedures. Please let us know if you need assistance or accommodations due to a disability."},{"id":"1a29f42d-e446-4ea0-a4f6-c3886e71ba7d","title":"Customer Support Developer (Databases)","department":"Technical Support ","team":"Technical Support ","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Canada","secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-10-08T18:32:05.448+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Canada"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/airbyte/1a29f42d-e446-4ea0-a4f6-c3886e71ba7d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/airbyte/1a29f42d-e446-4ea0-a4f6-c3886e71ba7d/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Airbyte is the data and action layer for AI agents. We give agents fast, accurate, authenticated access to business data across hundreds of sources, so they can discover the entities that matter, reason over real-time context, and take action in the systems they read from, not just observe them.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We started as the open-source standard for data movement and proved the economics of data integration at scale: hundreds of connectors, thousands of companies, and, since 2020, have raised $181M from leading investors including Benchmark, Accel, Altimeter, Coatue, and Y Combinator. As our CEO Michel Tricot puts it, \"the last ten years were all about structured data. The future is all about context.\" We're now building that context infrastructure for production-grade agents on the same open foundation, as agents become the primary consumers of enterprise data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our mission is unchanged: make data available and actionable to everyone, everywhere. That everyone now includes AI agents.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>The Role:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Are you the kind of developer who gets a rush from cracking a gnarly replication bug, an issue with CDC implementation, or a query that hangs with no obvious reason? Do you thrive at the intersection of writing code and helping customers succeed? As a Customer Support Developer (Databases) at Airbyte, you'll combine hands-on development skills with deep technical empathy to support our growing cloud, embedded, and open-source integration platform. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This isn't a traditional support role. You'll be writing Java and Kotlin, shipping contributions to our open-source database source and destination connectors, digging into query plans and transaction logs, and directly shaping how customers move mission-critical data between databases, warehouses, and lakes. You'll champion the customer voice alongside our engineering and product teams every day, getting your hands dirty in the code.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What You’ll Do:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Customer Support &amp; Technical Troubleshooting</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the primary technical escalation point for database-related customer issues, responding via email, ticketing systems, and video calls with precision and clarity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Triage and prioritize incoming issues with urgency, consistently meeting SLA targets while leveraging AI tools to work smarter and resolve issues faster.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Dig into complex issues across relational databases, data warehouses, data lakes, and cloud object storage, not just finding workarounds but partnering with Engineering to root-cause and drive real fixes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reproduce customer-reported bugs by inspecting connector logs, query plans, replication slots, transaction logs, sync state, and destination table state, and document findings with enough technical detail for Engineering to act on immediately.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support customers through onboarding and troubleshooting for SSH tunnels, network configuration, database user permissions, CDC setup (WAL/binlog/redo logs), and warehouse/lake authentication.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Database Connector Development</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Get hands-on with customers building and debugging integrations, helping them navigate Airbyte's database sources and destinations with confidence, from authentication and SSL/SSH setup to CDC, schema evolution, incremental cursors, and typed destination tables.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Validate database version compatibility across supported engines and releases, maintain testing environments, and reproduce customer-reported behavior on real database and warehouse instances.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support customers writing to data warehouses (Snowflake, BigQuery, Redshift), data lakes and object storage (S3, GCS, Azure Blob, Databricks, Iceberg), and databases (Postgres, MySQL, MSSQL, ClickHouse), including schema evolution and typed-columns behavior.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help customers running database sources (PostgreSQL, MySQL, MSSQL, Oracle, MongoDB, and more) troubleshoot replication behavior, cursor selection, full-refresh vs. incremental vs. CDC trade-offs, and sync state recovery.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute directly to Airbyte's open-source database connectors and the Java/Kotlin Bulk CDK: fix bugs, improve error handling, harden schema-evolution and CDC paths, and submit pull requests to the Airbyte repository.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review and test community contributions to database sources and destinations, helping external contributors land high-quality changes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay sharp on Airbyte's connector catalog, new database and destination releases, and platform updates so your guidance is always accurate and timely.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cross-Functional Collaboration &amp; Enablement</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be the voice of the customer within Airbyte, working closely with Engineering and Product to surface issues, advocate for feature requests, and ensure customer pain points actually influence the database reliability and performance roadmap.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Solutions Engineering and Sales Engineering to provide white-glove technical onboarding for enterprise customers, including CDC architecture reviews, destination schema modeling, and production readiness assessments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Train and mentor Technical Support Engineers on database connector concepts, including JDBC fundamentals, CDC patterns, schema evolution, query optimization, destination typing and normalization, and the Airbyte protocol (spec, discover, check, read, write).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Sales and Customer Success for technical conversations, onboarding, and expansion efforts, bringing the kind of product depth that helps close and retain customers.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge, Process Improvement, &amp; AI </p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create and maintain internal and external knowledge base articles, troubleshooting guides, and database connector documentation to support scalability.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Document research and troubleshooting processes,( including CDC debugging, destination schema reconciliation, and performance tuning runbooks), to aid faster ticket resolution and team knowledge sharing.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify AI-driven opportunities for automation and process improvements that reduce support load and improve the customer experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Embrace AI-assisted workflows and contribute to developing playbooks and skills that encode repeatable troubleshooting procedures, connector debugging patterns, and onboarding Runbooks, enabling the team to scale expertise through automation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Spearhead initiatives to fill organizational or support gaps and take ownership of unique projects.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What You’ll Need:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years in software engineering, data engineering, technical support, DevOps, QA, or a similar role supporting developers or technical users.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency in SQL, with hands-on experience investigating query plans, isolation levels, and performance bottlenecks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency in Java or Kotlin. You must be able to read, write, and debug JVM-based connector code. You'll be contributing to database sources and destinations, the Bulk CDK, and automation tooling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with relational databases, data warehouses, or data lakes, including concepts like CDC (Change Data Capture), schema evolution, and query optimization.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with JDBC and common database drivers, and comfort debugging connection, authentication, SSL, and SSH tunnel issues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of cloud platforms (AWS, GCP, or Azure) and data integration concepts, including ELT/ETL workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong troubleshooting instincts, clear communication with both technical and non-technical stakeholders, and a growth mindset that keeps you improving even when things get hard.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">High tolerance for ambiguity and a natural self-starter.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Nice To Have:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with PostgreSQL, MySQL, MSSQL, Oracle, MongoDB, Snowflake, BigQuery, Redshift, ClickHouse, or similar relational and non-relational systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with data lakes and open table formats (Iceberg, Delta Lake), and cloud object storage (S3, GCS, Azure Blob).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with Airbyte's Bulk CDK or contributions to open-source database connectors.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with container orchestration tools like Kubernetes or Docker and multi-tenant architectures.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background supporting developer-facing or embedded/platform products in a B2B SaaS context.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with CI/CD pipelines and GitHub-based open-source workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with AI-assisted development tools and building automated playbooks or Runbooks.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Location:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remote in Canada (Pacific, Mountain, Central timezones)</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Why You'll Love Working at Airbyte:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Airbyte, we believe great work happens when people feel supported, trusted, and empowered to grow. Our market-leading Total Rewards package is designed to help you thrive professionally and personally. Our benefits and perks include:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible PTO with a culture that encourages at least 25 days off annually, and public holidays in line with provincial employment standards</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comprehensive health coverage – extended health benefits on top of provincial public healthcare</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Virtual healthcare – access to doctors and other care providers online, so you can get care without waiting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Retirement savings – a group retirement savings plan to help you build for the future</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Statutory protections – Canada/Québec Pension Plan, Employment Insurance and workers' compensation coverage</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional development budget, conference sponsorship, and book reimbursement</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you find this role exciting, we encourage you to apply even if you think you don’t meet all of the requirements!</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are not accepting agency submissions or recruiting firm support for this role. Unsolicited resumes will not be considered.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Airbyte is the data and action layer for AI agents. We give agents fast, accurate, authenticated access to business data across hundreds of sources, so they can discover the entities that matter, reason over real-time context, and take action in the systems they read from, not just observe them.\n\n\n\nWe started as the open-source standard for data movement and proved the economics of data integration at scale: hundreds of connectors, thousands of companies, and, since 2020, have raised $181M from leading investors including Benchmark, Accel, Altimeter, Coatue, and Y Combinator. As our CEO Michel Tricot puts it, \"the last ten years were all about structured data. The future is all about context.\" We're now building that context infrastructure for production-grade agents on the same open foundation, as agents become the primary consumers of enterprise data.\n\n\n\nOur mission is unchanged: make data available and actionable to everyone, everywhere. That everyone now includes AI agents.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE:\n\nAre you the kind of developer who gets a rush from cracking a gnarly replication bug, an issue with CDC implementation, or a query that hangs with no obvious reason? Do you thrive at the intersection of writing code and helping customers succeed? As a Customer Support Developer (Databases) at Airbyte, you'll combine hands-on development skills with deep technical empathy to support our growing cloud, embedded, and open-source integration platform. \n\n\n\nThis isn't a traditional support role. You'll be writing Java and Kotlin, shipping contributions to our open-source database source and destination connectors, digging into query plans and transaction logs, and directly shaping how customers move mission-critical data between databases, warehouses, and lakes. You'll champion the customer voice alongside our engineering and product teams every day, getting your hands dirty in the code.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO:\n\nCustomer Support & Technical Troubleshooting\n\n - Serve as the primary technical escalation point for database-related customer issues, responding via email, ticketing systems, and video calls with precision and clarity.\n\n - Triage and prioritize incoming issues with urgency, consistently meeting SLA targets while leveraging AI tools to work smarter and resolve issues faster.\n\n - Dig into complex issues across relational databases, data warehouses, data lakes, and cloud object storage, not just finding workarounds but partnering with Engineering to root-cause and drive real fixes.\n\n - Reproduce customer-reported bugs by inspecting connector logs, query plans, replication slots, transaction logs, sync state, and destination table state, and document findings with enough technical detail for Engineering to act on immediately.\n\n - Support customers through onboarding and troubleshooting for SSH tunnels, network configuration, database user permissions, CDC setup (WAL/binlog/redo logs), and warehouse/lake authentication.\n\n\n\nDatabase Connector Development\n\n - Get hands-on with customers building and debugging integrations, helping them navigate Airbyte's database sources and destinations with confidence, from authentication and SSL/SSH setup to CDC, schema evolution, incremental cursors, and typed destination tables.\n\n - Validate database version compatibility across supported engines and releases, maintain testing environments, and reproduce customer-reported behavior on real database and warehouse instances.\n\n - Support customers writing to data warehouses (Snowflake, BigQuery, Redshift), data lakes and object storage (S3, GCS, Azure Blob, Databricks, Iceberg), and databases (Postgres, MySQL, MSSQL, ClickHouse), including schema evolution and typed-columns behavior.\n\n - Help customers running database sources (PostgreSQL, MySQL, MSSQL, Oracle, MongoDB, and more) troubleshoot replication behavior, cursor selection, full-refresh vs. incremental vs. CDC trade-offs, and sync state recovery.\n\n - Contribute directly to Airbyte's open-source database connectors and the Java/Kotlin Bulk CDK: fix bugs, improve error handling, harden schema-evolution and CDC paths, and submit pull requests to the Airbyte repository.\n\n - Review and test community contributions to database sources and destinations, helping external contributors land high-quality changes.\n\n - Stay sharp on Airbyte's connector catalog, new database and destination releases, and platform updates so your guidance is always accurate and timely.\n\n\n\nCross-Functional Collaboration & Enablement\n\n - Be the voice of the customer within Airbyte, working closely with Engineering and Product to surface issues, advocate for feature requests, and ensure customer pain points actually influence the database reliability and performance roadmap.\n\n - Partner with Solutions Engineering and Sales Engineering to provide white-glove technical onboarding for enterprise customers, including CDC architecture reviews, destination schema modeling, and production readiness assessments.\n\n - Train and mentor Technical Support Engineers on database connector concepts, including JDBC fundamentals, CDC patterns, schema evolution, query optimization, destination typing and normalization, and the Airbyte protocol (spec, discover, check, read, write).\n\n - Partner with Sales and Customer Success for technical conversations, onboarding, and expansion efforts, bringing the kind of product depth that helps close and retain customers.\n\n\n\nKnowledge, Process Improvement, & AI \n\n - Create and maintain internal and external knowledge base articles, troubleshooting guides, and database connector documentation to support scalability.\n\n - Document research and troubleshooting processes,( including CDC debugging, destination schema reconciliation, and performance tuning runbooks), to aid faster ticket resolution and team knowledge sharing.\n\n - Identify AI-driven opportunities for automation and process improvements that reduce support load and improve the customer experience.\n\n - Embrace AI-assisted workflows and contribute to developing playbooks and skills that encode repeatable troubleshooting procedures, connector debugging patterns, and onboarding Runbooks, enabling the team to scale expertise through automation.\n\n - Spearhead initiatives to fill organizational or support gaps and take ownership of unique projects.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL NEED:\n\n - 2+ years in software engineering, data engineering, technical support, DevOps, QA, or a similar role supporting developers or technical users.\n\n - Fluency in SQL, with hands-on experience investigating query plans, isolation levels, and performance bottlenecks.\n\n - Proficiency in Java or Kotlin. You must be able to read, write, and debug JVM-based connector code. You'll be contributing to database sources and destinations, the Bulk CDK, and automation tooling.\n\n - Hands-on experience with relational databases, data warehouses, or data lakes, including concepts like CDC (Change Data Capture), schema evolution, and query optimization.\n\n - Experience with JDBC and common database drivers, and comfort debugging connection, authentication, SSL, and SSH tunnel issues.\n\n - Understanding of cloud platforms (AWS, GCP, or Azure) and data integration concepts, including ELT/ETL workflows.\n\n - Strong troubleshooting instincts, clear communication with both technical and non-technical stakeholders, and a growth mindset that keeps you improving even when things get hard.\n\n - High tolerance for ambiguity and a natural self-starter.\n\n\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE:\n\n - Experience with PostgreSQL, MySQL, MSSQL, Oracle, MongoDB, Snowflake, BigQuery, Redshift, ClickHouse, or similar relational and non-relational systems.\n\n - Experience with data lakes and open table formats (Iceberg, Delta Lake), and cloud object storage (S3, GCS, Azure Blob).\n\n - Familiarity with Airbyte's Bulk CDK or contributions to open-source database connectors.\n\n - Experience with container orchestration tools like Kubernetes or Docker and multi-tenant architectures.\n\n - Background supporting developer-facing or embedded/platform products in a B2B SaaS context.\n\n - Experience with CI/CD pipelines and GitHub-based open-source workflows.\n\n - Experience with AI-assisted development tools and building automated playbooks or Runbooks.\n\n\n\n\nLOCATION:\n\n - Remote in Canada (Pacific, Mountain, Central timezones)\n\n\n\n\nWHY YOU'LL LOVE WORKING AT AIRBYTE:\n\nAt Airbyte, we believe great work happens when people feel supported, trusted, and empowered to grow. Our market-leading Total Rewards package is designed to help you thrive professionally and personally. Our benefits and perks include:\n\n - Flexible PTO with a culture that encourages at least 25 days off annually, and public holidays in line with provincial employment standards\n\n - Comprehensive health coverage – extended health benefits on top of provincial public healthcare\n\n - Virtual healthcare – access to doctors and other care providers online, so you can get care without waiting\n\n - Retirement savings – a group retirement savings plan to help you build for the future\n\n - Statutory protections – Canada/Québec Pension Plan, Employment Insurance and workers' compensation coverage\n\n - Professional development budget, conference sponsorship, and book reimbursement\n\n\n\nIf you find this role exciting, we encourage you to apply even if you think you don’t meet all of the requirements!\n\n \n\nWe are not accepting agency submissions or recruiting firm support for this role. Unsolicited resumes will not be considered."},{"id":"9af619c8-163a-4170-bac6-6ceee93558fe","title":"Enterprise Account Executive","department":"Sales","team":"Sales","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Canada","secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-10-08T18:48:45.570+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Canada"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/airbyte/9af619c8-163a-4170-bac6-6ceee93558fe","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/airbyte/9af619c8-163a-4170-bac6-6ceee93558fe/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Airbyte is the data and action layer for AI agents. We give agents fast, accurate, authenticated access to business data across hundreds of sources, so they can discover the entities that matter, reason over real-time context, and take action in the systems they read from, not just observe them.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We started as the open-source standard for data movement and proved the economics of data integration at scale: hundreds of connectors, thousands of companies, and, since 2020, have raised $181M from leading investors including Benchmark, Accel, Altimeter, Coatue, and Y Combinator. As our CEO Michel Tricot puts it, \"the last ten years were all about structured data. The future is all about context.\" We're now building that context infrastructure for production-grade agents on the same open foundation, as agents become the primary consumers of enterprise data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our mission is unchanged: make data available and actionable to everyone, everywhere. That everyone now includes AI agents.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>The Role:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Airbyte is seeking an experienced Enterprise Account Executive to join our growing sales organization. In this role, you will own a defined portfolio of enterprise accounts and be responsible for generating, progressing, and closing new business across Airbyte’s product offerings.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will work a mix of qualified inbound opportunities and strategically selected target accounts, while building relationships and creating demand across your territory. You will primarily engage with CTO, CIO, data, and engineering organizations, working with stakeholders ranging from data engineers and architects to senior business and technology executives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A successful candidate will be comfortable navigating complex technical environments, leading multi-stakeholder sales processes, and connecting technical capabilities to measurable business outcomes. A foundational understanding of cloud infrastructure, the modern data stack, APIs, data integration, and database replication is strongly preferred. Candidates with a demonstrated ability to quickly learn complex technical concepts will also be considered.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a new-business-focused role. Success will be driven by landing strategic customers, establishing Airbyte within an initial use case, and creating a clear path toward broader adoption across the organization. You will join a fast-growing company with a strong product-led motion, a highly technical customer base, and a significant market opportunity.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h2><strong>What You’ll Do:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the full enterprise sales cycle, from account development and discovery through technical evaluation, proposal, negotiation, procurement, and closed-won.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain a healthy pipeline through a combination of qualified inbound opportunities, targeted outbound prospecting, partner engagement, and strategic account development.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop trusted relationships across technical, business, and executive stakeholders within enterprise accounts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead effective discovery to uncover customer challenges, business priorities, technical requirements, and decision criteria.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Apply value-selling principles and Airbyte’s sales methodology, including Command of the Message and MEDDPICC, to quantify customer pain, establish urgency, differentiate Airbyte, and maintain control of the sales process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build clear and compelling business cases that connect Airbyte’s technical capabilities to measurable customer outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with Solutions Engineering to scope, manage, and successfully complete technical evaluations and proofs of value.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Navigate complex security, legal, procurement, and commercial processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create account strategies that support both initial adoption and long-term expansion.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate opportunity, pipeline, MEDDPICC, and forecast information.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Consistently achieve or exceed quarterly bookings targets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with Product, Marketing, Engineering, Customer Success, and other internal teams to share market feedback, competitive intelligence, customer requirements, and product opportunities.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h2><strong>What You’ll Need:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3-5+ years of B2B sales experience within SaaS, cloud infrastructure, developer tools, or data technology, including at least 1-2+ years selling into enterprise accounts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A demonstrated history of meeting or exceeding quota in a new-business sales role.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing complex, multi-stakeholder enterprise sales cycles.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience using structured enterprise sales methodologies such as Command of the Message, MEDDPICC, and value-based selling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A proven ability to uncover and quantify business pain, build compelling value propositions, establish urgency, and navigate enterprise decision-making processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Confidence engaging both technical practitioners and executive buyers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ability to translate complex technical capabilities into clear business value.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong prospecting, discovery, presentation, negotiation, and communication skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent organization, pipeline management, and forecasting discipline.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Direct experience with data infrastructure, cloud platforms, data integration, or the modern data stack is strongly preferred.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A proactive, curious, accountable, and collaborative working style.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ability to operate effectively in a fast-paced and evolving environment.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h2><strong>Location:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remote in Canada (Central and Eastern timezone)</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Why You'll Love Working at Airbyte:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Airbyte, we believe great work happens when people feel supported, trusted, and empowered to grow. Our market-leading Total Rewards package is designed to help you thrive professionally and personally. Our benefits and perks include:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible PTO with a culture that encourages at least 25 days off annually, and public holidays in line with provincial employment standards</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comprehensive health coverage – extended health benefits on top of provincial public healthcare</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Virtual healthcare – access to doctors and other care providers online, so you can get care without waiting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Retirement savings – a group retirement savings plan to help you build for the future</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Statutory protections – Canada/Québec Pension Plan, Employment Insurance and workers' compensation coverage</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional development budget, conference sponsorship, and book reimbursement</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you find this role exciting, we encourage you to apply even if you think you don’t meet all of the requirements!</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are not accepting agency submissions or recruiting firm support for this role. Unsolicited resumes will not be considered.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Airbyte is the data and action layer for AI agents. We give agents fast, accurate, authenticated access to business data across hundreds of sources, so they can discover the entities that matter, reason over real-time context, and take action in the systems they read from, not just observe them.\n\n\n\nWe started as the open-source standard for data movement and proved the economics of data integration at scale: hundreds of connectors, thousands of companies, and, since 2020, have raised $181M from leading investors including Benchmark, Accel, Altimeter, Coatue, and Y Combinator. As our CEO Michel Tricot puts it, \"the last ten years were all about structured data. The future is all about context.\" We're now building that context infrastructure for production-grade agents on the same open foundation, as agents become the primary consumers of enterprise data.\n\n\n\nOur mission is unchanged: make data available and actionable to everyone, everywhere. That everyone now includes AI agents.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE:\n\nAirbyte is seeking an experienced Enterprise Account Executive to join our growing sales organization. In this role, you will own a defined portfolio of enterprise accounts and be responsible for generating, progressing, and closing new business across Airbyte’s product offerings.\n\n\n\nYou will work a mix of qualified inbound opportunities and strategically selected target accounts, while building relationships and creating demand across your territory. You will primarily engage with CTO, CIO, data, and engineering organizations, working with stakeholders ranging from data engineers and architects to senior business and technology executives.\n\n\n\nA successful candidate will be comfortable navigating complex technical environments, leading multi-stakeholder sales processes, and connecting technical capabilities to measurable business outcomes. A foundational understanding of cloud infrastructure, the modern data stack, APIs, data integration, and database replication is strongly preferred. Candidates with a demonstrated ability to quickly learn complex technical concepts will also be considered.\n\n\n\nThis is a new-business-focused role. Success will be driven by landing strategic customers, establishing Airbyte within an initial use case, and creating a clear path toward broader adoption across the organization. You will join a fast-growing company with a strong product-led motion, a highly technical customer base, and a significant market opportunity.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO:\n\n - Own the full enterprise sales cycle, from account development and discovery through technical evaluation, proposal, negotiation, procurement, and closed-won.\n\n - Build and maintain a healthy pipeline through a combination of qualified inbound opportunities, targeted outbound prospecting, partner engagement, and strategic account development.\n\n - Develop trusted relationships across technical, business, and executive stakeholders within enterprise accounts.\n\n - Lead effective discovery to uncover customer challenges, business priorities, technical requirements, and decision criteria.\n\n - Apply value-selling principles and Airbyte’s sales methodology, including Command of the Message and MEDDPICC, to quantify customer pain, establish urgency, differentiate Airbyte, and maintain control of the sales process.\n\n - Build clear and compelling business cases that connect Airbyte’s technical capabilities to measurable customer outcomes.\n\n - Partner closely with Solutions Engineering to scope, manage, and successfully complete technical evaluations and proofs of value.\n\n - Navigate complex security, legal, procurement, and commercial processes.\n\n - Create account strategies that support both initial adoption and long-term expansion.\n\n - Maintain accurate opportunity, pipeline, MEDDPICC, and forecast information.\n\n - Consistently achieve or exceed quarterly bookings targets.\n\n - Collaborate with Product, Marketing, Engineering, Customer Success, and other internal teams to share market feedback, competitive intelligence, customer requirements, and product opportunities.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL NEED:\n\n - 3-5+ years of B2B sales experience within SaaS, cloud infrastructure, developer tools, or data technology, including at least 1-2+ years selling into enterprise accounts.\n\n - A demonstrated history of meeting or exceeding quota in a new-business sales role.\n\n - Experience managing complex, multi-stakeholder enterprise sales cycles.\n\n - Experience using structured enterprise sales methodologies such as Command of the Message, MEDDPICC, and value-based selling.\n\n - A proven ability to uncover and quantify business pain, build compelling value propositions, establish urgency, and navigate enterprise decision-making processes.\n\n - Confidence engaging both technical practitioners and executive buyers.\n\n - The ability to translate complex technical capabilities into clear business value.\n\n - Strong prospecting, discovery, presentation, negotiation, and communication skills.\n\n - Excellent organization, pipeline management, and forecasting discipline.\n\n - Direct experience with data infrastructure, cloud platforms, data integration, or the modern data stack is strongly preferred.\n\n - A proactive, curious, accountable, and collaborative working style.\n\n - The ability to operate effectively in a fast-paced and evolving environment.\n\n \n\n\nLOCATION:\n\n - Remote in Canada (Central and Eastern timezone)\n\n\n\n\nWHY YOU'LL LOVE WORKING AT AIRBYTE:\n\nAt Airbyte, we believe great work happens when people feel supported, trusted, and empowered to grow. Our market-leading Total Rewards package is designed to help you thrive professionally and personally. Our benefits and perks include:\n\n - Flexible PTO with a culture that encourages at least 25 days off annually, and public holidays in line with provincial employment standards\n\n - Comprehensive health coverage – extended health benefits on top of provincial public healthcare\n\n - Virtual healthcare – access to doctors and other care providers online, so you can get care without waiting\n\n - Retirement savings – a group retirement savings plan to help you build for the future\n\n - Statutory protections – Canada/Québec Pension Plan, Employment Insurance and workers' compensation coverage\n\n - Professional development budget, conference sponsorship, and book reimbursement\n\n \n\nIf you find this role exciting, we encourage you to apply even if you think you don’t meet all of the requirements!\n\n \n\nWe are not accepting agency submissions or recruiting firm support for this role. Unsolicited resumes will not be considered."},{"id":"5e394a39-58d4-43a6-9ce3-3c009a7362c8","title":"Enterprise Account Executive","department":"Sales","team":"Sales","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"United States","secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-10-08T18:48:42.621+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/airbyte/5e394a39-58d4-43a6-9ce3-3c009a7362c8","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/airbyte/5e394a39-58d4-43a6-9ce3-3c009a7362c8/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Airbyte is the data and action layer for AI agents. We give agents fast, accurate, authenticated access to business data across hundreds of sources, so they can discover the entities that matter, reason over real-time context, and take action in the systems they read from, not just observe them.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We started as the open-source standard for data movement and proved the economics of data integration at scale: hundreds of connectors, thousands of companies, and, since 2020, have raised $181M from leading investors including Benchmark, Accel, Altimeter, Coatue, and Y Combinator. As our CEO Michel Tricot puts it, \"the last ten years were all about structured data. The future is all about context.\" We're now building that context infrastructure for production-grade agents on the same open foundation, as agents become the primary consumers of enterprise data.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our mission is unchanged: make data available and actionable to everyone, everywhere. That everyone now includes AI agents.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>The Role:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Airbyte is seeking an experienced Enterprise Account Executive to join our growing sales organization. In this role, you will own a defined portfolio of enterprise accounts and be responsible for generating, progressing, and closing new business across Airbyte’s product offerings.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will work a mix of qualified inbound opportunities and strategically selected target accounts, while building relationships and creating demand across your territory. You will primarily engage with CTO, CIO, data, and engineering organizations, working with stakeholders ranging from data engineers and architects to senior business and technology executives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A successful candidate will be comfortable navigating complex technical environments, leading multi-stakeholder sales processes, and connecting technical capabilities to measurable business outcomes. A foundational understanding of cloud infrastructure, the modern data stack, APIs, data integration, and database replication is strongly preferred. Candidates with a demonstrated ability to quickly learn complex technical concepts will also be considered.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a new-business-focused role. Success will be driven by landing strategic customers, establishing Airbyte within an initial use case, and creating a clear path toward broader adoption across the organization. You will join a fast-growing company with a strong product-led motion, a highly technical customer base, and a significant market opportunity.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h2><strong>What You’ll Do:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the full enterprise sales cycle, from account development and discovery through technical evaluation, proposal, negotiation, procurement, and closed-won.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain a healthy pipeline through a combination of qualified inbound opportunities, targeted outbound prospecting, partner engagement, and strategic account development.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop trusted relationships across technical, business, and executive stakeholders within enterprise accounts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead effective discovery to uncover customer challenges, business priorities, technical requirements, and decision criteria.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Apply value-selling principles and Airbyte’s sales methodology, including Command of the Message and MEDDPICC, to quantify customer pain, establish urgency, differentiate Airbyte, and maintain control of the sales process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build clear and compelling business cases that connect Airbyte’s technical capabilities to measurable customer outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with Solutions Engineering to scope, manage, and successfully complete technical evaluations and proofs of value.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Navigate complex security, legal, procurement, and commercial processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create account strategies that support both initial adoption and long-term expansion.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate opportunity, pipeline, MEDDPICC, and forecast information.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Consistently achieve or exceed quarterly bookings targets.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with Product, Marketing, Engineering, Customer Success, and other internal teams to share market feedback, competitive intelligence, customer requirements, and product opportunities.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h2><strong>What You’ll Need:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3-5+ years of B2B sales experience within SaaS, cloud infrastructure, developer tools, or data technology, including at least 1-2+ years selling into enterprise accounts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A demonstrated history of meeting or exceeding quota in a new-business sales role.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing complex, multi-stakeholder enterprise sales cycles.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience using structured enterprise sales methodologies such as Command of the Message, MEDDPICC, and value-based selling.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A proven ability to uncover and quantify business pain, build compelling value propositions, establish urgency, and navigate enterprise decision-making processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Confidence engaging both technical practitioners and executive buyers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ability to translate complex technical capabilities into clear business value.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong prospecting, discovery, presentation, negotiation, and communication skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent organization, pipeline management, and forecasting discipline.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Direct experience with data infrastructure, cloud platforms, data integration, or the modern data stack is strongly preferred.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A proactive, curious, accountable, and collaborative working style.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ability to operate effectively in a fast-paced and evolving environment.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h2><strong>Location:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remote in U.S. (Central and Eastern timezone)</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Why You'll Love Working at Airbyte:</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Airbyte, we believe great work happens when people feel supported, trusted, and empowered to grow. Our market-leading Total Rewards package is designed to help you thrive professionally and personally. Our benefits and perks include:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible PTO with a culture that encourages at least 25 days off annually, and public holidays in line with provincial employment standards</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comprehensive health coverage – extended health benefits on top of provincial public healthcare</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Virtual healthcare – access to doctors and other care providers online, so you can get care without waiting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Retirement savings – a group retirement savings plan to help you build for the future</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Statutory protections – Canada/Québec Pension Plan, Employment Insurance and workers' compensation coverage</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional development budget, conference sponsorship, and book reimbursement</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you find this role exciting, we encourage you to apply even if you think you don’t meet all of the requirements!</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are not accepting agency submissions or recruiting firm support for this role. Unsolicited resumes will not be considered.</p>","descriptionPlain":"Airbyte is the data and action layer for AI agents. We give agents fast, accurate, authenticated access to business data across hundreds of sources, so they can discover the entities that matter, reason over real-time context, and take action in the systems they read from, not just observe them.\n\n\n\nWe started as the open-source standard for data movement and proved the economics of data integration at scale: hundreds of connectors, thousands of companies, and, since 2020, have raised $181M from leading investors including Benchmark, Accel, Altimeter, Coatue, and Y Combinator. As our CEO Michel Tricot puts it, \"the last ten years were all about structured data. The future is all about context.\" We're now building that context infrastructure for production-grade agents on the same open foundation, as agents become the primary consumers of enterprise data.\n\n\n\nOur mission is unchanged: make data available and actionable to everyone, everywhere. That everyone now includes AI agents.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE:\n\nAirbyte is seeking an experienced Enterprise Account Executive to join our growing sales organization. In this role, you will own a defined portfolio of enterprise accounts and be responsible for generating, progressing, and closing new business across Airbyte’s product offerings.\n\n\n\nYou will work a mix of qualified inbound opportunities and strategically selected target accounts, while building relationships and creating demand across your territory. You will primarily engage with CTO, CIO, data, and engineering organizations, working with stakeholders ranging from data engineers and architects to senior business and technology executives.\n\n\n\nA successful candidate will be comfortable navigating complex technical environments, leading multi-stakeholder sales processes, and connecting technical capabilities to measurable business outcomes. A foundational understanding of cloud infrastructure, the modern data stack, APIs, data integration, and database replication is strongly preferred. Candidates with a demonstrated ability to quickly learn complex technical concepts will also be considered.\n\n\n\nThis is a new-business-focused role. Success will be driven by landing strategic customers, establishing Airbyte within an initial use case, and creating a clear path toward broader adoption across the organization. You will join a fast-growing company with a strong product-led motion, a highly technical customer base, and a significant market opportunity.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO:\n\n - Own the full enterprise sales cycle, from account development and discovery through technical evaluation, proposal, negotiation, procurement, and closed-won.\n\n - Build and maintain a healthy pipeline through a combination of qualified inbound opportunities, targeted outbound prospecting, partner engagement, and strategic account development.\n\n - Develop trusted relationships across technical, business, and executive stakeholders within enterprise accounts.\n\n - Lead effective discovery to uncover customer challenges, business priorities, technical requirements, and decision criteria.\n\n - Apply value-selling principles and Airbyte’s sales methodology, including Command of the Message and MEDDPICC, to quantify customer pain, establish urgency, differentiate Airbyte, and maintain control of the sales process.\n\n - Build clear and compelling business cases that connect Airbyte’s technical capabilities to measurable customer outcomes.\n\n - Partner closely with Solutions Engineering to scope, manage, and successfully complete technical evaluations and proofs of value.\n\n - Navigate complex security, legal, procurement, and commercial processes.\n\n - Create account strategies that support both initial adoption and long-term expansion.\n\n - Maintain accurate opportunity, pipeline, MEDDPICC, and forecast information.\n\n - Consistently achieve or exceed quarterly bookings targets.\n\n - Collaborate with Product, Marketing, Engineering, Customer Success, and other internal teams to share market feedback, competitive intelligence, customer requirements, and product opportunities.\n\n \n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL NEED:\n\n - 3-5+ years of B2B sales experience within SaaS, cloud infrastructure, developer tools, or data technology, including at least 1-2+ years selling into enterprise accounts.\n\n - A demonstrated history of meeting or exceeding quota in a new-business sales role.\n\n - Experience managing complex, multi-stakeholder enterprise sales cycles.\n\n - Experience using structured enterprise sales methodologies such as Command of the Message, MEDDPICC, and value-based selling.\n\n - A proven ability to uncover and quantify business pain, build compelling value propositions, establish urgency, and navigate enterprise decision-making processes.\n\n - Confidence engaging both technical practitioners and executive buyers.\n\n - The ability to translate complex technical capabilities into clear business value.\n\n - Strong prospecting, discovery, presentation, negotiation, and communication skills.\n\n - Excellent organization, pipeline management, and forecasting discipline.\n\n - Direct experience with data infrastructure, cloud platforms, data integration, or the modern data stack is strongly preferred.\n\n - A proactive, curious, accountable, and collaborative working style.\n\n - The ability to operate effectively in a fast-paced and evolving environment.\n\n \n\n\nLOCATION:\n\n - Remote in U.S. (Central and Eastern timezone)\n\n\n\n\nWHY YOU'LL LOVE WORKING AT AIRBYTE:\n\nAt Airbyte, we believe great work happens when people feel supported, trusted, and empowered to grow. Our market-leading Total Rewards package is designed to help you thrive professionally and personally. Our benefits and perks include:\n\n - Flexible PTO with a culture that encourages at least 25 days off annually, and public holidays in line with provincial employment standards\n\n - Comprehensive health coverage – extended health benefits on top of provincial public healthcare\n\n - Virtual healthcare – access to doctors and other care providers online, so you can get care without waiting\n\n - Retirement savings – a group retirement savings plan to help you build for the future\n\n - Statutory protections – Canada/Québec Pension Plan, Employment Insurance and workers' compensation coverage\n\n - Professional development budget, conference sponsorship, and book reimbursement\n\n \n\nIf you find this role exciting, we encourage you to apply even if you think you don’t meet all of the requirements!\n\n \n\nWe are not accepting agency submissions or recruiting firm support for this role. Unsolicited resumes will not be considered."}],"apiVersion":"1"}